0
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
BLACK SCREEN

1
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:56,750
I don't know about you, it's just too hot today, isn't it?

2
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:59,010
And it's going to get even worse.

3
00:00:59,010 --> 00:01:01,260
Temperatures up in the mid-30s Celsius...

4
00:01:01,270 --> 00:01:05,130
...that's the mid-90s Fahrenheit, tomorrow, maybe even hitting 100.

5
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:07,970
So, please, remember to cover up and stay cool...

6
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:10,970
...with the hottest hits on your FM dial.

7
00:01:10,980 --> 00:01:14,010
Come on, guys, time to go home.

8
00:01:14,480 --> 00:01:16,880
Come on, love, off you get.

9
00:01:18,550 --> 00:01:22,290
-Do we have to? -Yes, we do.

10
00:01:22,590 --> 00:01:25,830
I'll make you your favorite dinner to compensate.

11
00:01:26,890 --> 00:01:28,720
He squealed like a pig, didn't he?

12
00:01:28,730 --> 00:01:32,420
Yeah, brilliant punch, Big D. Did you see his face?

13
00:01:32,430 --> 00:01:34,560
Hey, Big D.

14
00:01:35,170 --> 00:01:36,960
Beat up another 10-year-old?

15
00:01:36,970 --> 00:01:39,760
-This one deserved it. -Yeah.

16
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:44,440
-Five against one, very brave. -Well, you're one to talk.

17
00:01:44,450 --> 00:01:46,580
Moaning in your sleep every night?

18
00:01:46,590 --> 00:01:49,190
At least I'm not afraid of my pillow.

19
00:01:51,890 --> 00:01:55,020
"Don't kill cedric."

20
00:01:55,160 --> 00:01:57,220
Who's cedric, your boyfriend?

21
00:01:58,160 --> 00:02:02,420
-Shut up. -He's going to kill me, Mum.

22
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:05,090
Where is your mum?

23
00:02:05,630 --> 00:02:08,560
Where is your mum, Potter?

24
00:02:08,740 --> 00:02:10,800
She dead?

25
00:02:11,670 --> 00:02:13,600
Is she dead?

26
00:02:13,810 --> 00:02:15,470
Is she a dead Pott...?

27
00:02:29,390 --> 00:02:31,490
-Dudley. -Dudley, let's go.

28
00:02:34,100 --> 00:02:36,090
-What's going on? -What are you doing?

29
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:39,220
-I'm not doing anything. -We're getting out of here, Dudley.

30
00:02:39,230 --> 00:02:41,060
Come on, Dudley, hurry up.

31
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:33,350
Dudley, run.

32
00:04:08,720 --> 00:04:10,420
Expecto Patronum.

33
00:04:39,990 --> 00:04:42,050
Mrs. Figg.

34
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:48,020
Don't put away your wand, Harry.

35
00:04:48,030 --> 00:04:50,700
They might come back.

36
00:04:51,700 --> 00:04:54,790
Dementors in Little whinging, whatever next?

37
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:56,630
-Whole world's gone topsy-turvy.

38
00:04:56,640 --> 00:04:58,930
-I don't understand. How do you know...?

39
00:04:58,940 --> 00:05:01,300
Dumbledore asked me to keep an eye on you.

40
00:05:01,310 --> 00:05:04,870
Dumbledore asked you? You know Dumbledore?

41
00:05:04,880 --> 00:05:08,870
After You-Know-who killed that poor Diggory boy last year...

42
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:11,710
...did you expect him to let you go wandering on your own?

43
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:14,550
Good Lord, boy. They told me you were intelligent.

44
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:17,850
Now, get inside and stay there.

45
00:05:17,860 --> 00:05:19,240
Expect someone will be in touch soon.

46
00:05:19,250 --> 00:05:22,130
Whatever happens, don't leave the house.

47
00:05:31,940 --> 00:05:34,470
It is hot. That's right, hot everywhere.

48
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:36,770
There's sweat. There's stifling.

49
00:05:36,780 --> 00:05:38,980
Diddykins?

50
00:05:39,010 --> 00:05:41,340
Is that you?

51
00:05:44,250 --> 00:05:47,680
Duddy. Vernon, come quick.

52
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:50,750
We're going to have to take him to a hospital.

53
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:53,190
Who did this to you, boy?

54
00:05:57,300 --> 00:05:59,360
Happy, are we, now?

55
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:03,230
You've finally done it. You've finally driven him loopy.

56
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:06,200
Vernon, don't say that.

57
00:06:06,210 --> 00:06:10,880
Well, just look at him, Petunia. Our boy has gone yumpy.

58
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:13,070
I've reached my limit, do you hear?

59
00:06:13,080 --> 00:06:17,210
This is the last I'm gonna take of you and your nonsense.

60
00:06:30,830 --> 00:06:33,090
-Dear Mr. Potter. -What?

61
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:38,500
The Ministry has received intelligence that at 6:23 this evening...

62
00:06:38,510 --> 00:06:43,470
...you performed the Patronus charm in the presence of a Muggle.

63
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:45,670
As a clear violation...

64
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:49,910
...of the Decree for the Reasonable Restriction of Underage Sorcery...

65
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:52,340
...you are hereby expelled...

66
00:06:52,490 --> 00:06:56,240
...from Hogwarts School of witchcraft and wizardry.

67
00:06:56,660 --> 00:07:01,360
Hoping you are well, Mafalda Hopkirk.

68
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:07,830
Justice.

69
00:07:19,780 --> 00:07:22,280
He's not very well.

70
00:07:34,530 --> 00:07:36,590
Sorry, Hedwig.

71
00:08:43,500 --> 00:08:45,590
Very clean, these Muggles.

72
00:08:45,670 --> 00:08:48,830
-Tonks, for God's sake. -Unnatural.

73
00:08:52,510 --> 00:08:54,360
Professor Moody.

74
00:08:54,510 --> 00:08:57,830
-What are you doing here? -Rescuing you, of course.

75
00:09:00,450 --> 00:09:03,310
But where are we going? The letter said I've been expelled.

76
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:05,910
You haven't been. Not yet. Kingsley, you take point.

77
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:07,080
But the letter said...

78
00:09:07,090 --> 00:09:10,280
Dumbledore persuaded the minister to suspend your expulsion...

79
00:09:10,290 --> 00:09:12,620
-...pending a formal hearing. -A hearing?

80
00:09:12,630 --> 00:09:16,150
Don't worry. We'll explain everything when we get back to headquarters.

81
00:09:16,160 --> 00:09:18,620
Not here, Nymphadora.

82
00:09:18,630 --> 00:09:22,770
Don't call me Nymphadora.

83
00:09:27,810 --> 00:09:32,240
Stay in formation, everyone. Don't break ranks if one of us is killed.

84
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:24,050
Come on, you, around the corner.

85
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:27,570
Come on.

86
00:11:06,710 --> 00:11:08,770
In you go, son.

87
00:11:10,010 --> 00:11:11,670
There've been no sightings.

88
00:11:11,680 --> 00:11:13,570
No deaths. No proof.

89
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:16,610
He almost killed Harry. If that isn't proof enough...

90
00:11:16,620 --> 00:11:20,850
Yes, but guarding you-know-what is the most important...

91
00:11:22,820 --> 00:11:25,420
we must trust Dumbledore on this.

92
00:11:25,430 --> 00:11:27,940
Was he able to protect Harry last year?

93
00:11:27,940 --> 00:11:29,990
Well, tonight I say it's time to take action.

94
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:33,360
Cornelius Fudge is a politician first and a wizard second.

95
00:11:33,370 --> 00:11:36,690
-His instinct would be to ignore it... -Keep your voices down.

96
00:11:36,700 --> 00:11:41,440
He's getting stronger and stronger by the minute. We have to act now.

97
00:11:45,110 --> 00:11:47,710
-Harry. -Mrs. Weasley.

98
00:11:50,050 --> 00:11:52,840
Heavens, you're all right.

99
00:11:56,060 --> 00:11:59,950
Bit peaky, but I'm afraid dinner will wait until after the meeting's finished.

100
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:05,390
Nope. No time to explain. Straight upstairs, first door on the left.

101
00:12:05,470 --> 00:12:07,200
Yeah.

102
00:12:09,170 --> 00:12:14,530
Mudblood, werewolves, traitors, thieves.

103
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:16,210
If my poor mistress knew

104
00:12:16,220 --> 00:12:19,390
the scum they let into her house...

105
00:12:19,580 --> 00:12:22,180
...what would she say to old Kreacher?

106
00:12:22,920 --> 00:12:26,210
Oh, the shame.

107
00:12:38,330 --> 00:12:41,230
Freaks. There, there, mistress.

108
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:44,800
Scum of the earth. Not like it was in the days of my fathers.

109
00:12:44,810 --> 00:12:47,700
Kreacher is here.

110
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:53,210
Oh, Harry.

111
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:59,710
Are you all right? We overheard them talking about the Dementor attack.

112
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:02,710
-You must tell us everything. -Let the man breathe, Hermione.

113
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:07,080
And this hearing at the Ministry. It's just outrageous.

114
00:13:07,090 --> 00:13:09,420
I've looked it up. They simply can't expel you.

115
00:13:09,430 --> 00:13:12,430
-It's completely unfair. -Yeah.

116
00:13:12,630 --> 00:13:15,560
There's a lot of that going round at the moment.

117
00:13:17,170 --> 00:13:19,260
So, what is this place?

118
00:13:19,270 --> 00:13:22,270
-It's headquarters. -Of the order of the Phoenix.

119
00:13:22,780 --> 00:13:24,440
It's a secret society.

120
00:13:24,450 --> 00:13:27,170
Dumbledore formed it back when they fought You-Know-who.

121
00:13:27,180 --> 00:13:30,040
Couldn't have put any of this in a letter, I suppose?

122
00:13:30,420 --> 00:13:32,910
I've gone all summer without a scrap of news.

123
00:13:33,220 --> 00:13:37,050
We wanted to write, mate. Really, we did.

124
00:13:37,060 --> 00:13:38,220
-Only... -Only what?

125
00:13:38,230 --> 00:13:41,720
Only Dumbledore made us swear not to tell you anything.

126
00:13:43,230 --> 00:13:45,230
Dumbledore said that?

127
00:13:46,730 --> 00:13:49,630
But why would he keep me in the dark? Maybe I could help.

128
00:13:49,640 --> 00:13:51,760
I'm the one who saw Voldemort return...

129
00:13:51,770 --> 00:13:54,770
...the one who fought him, who saw cedric Diggory get killed.

130
00:13:54,780 --> 00:13:57,130
-Harry. -Thought we heard your dulcet tones.

131
00:13:57,140 --> 00:13:59,650
-Don't bottle it up, though, mate. Let it out.

132
00:13:59,650 --> 00:14:01,370
-If you're all done shouting...

133
00:14:01,380 --> 00:14:04,170
Do you wanna hear something a little more interesting?

134
00:14:05,190 --> 00:14:08,680
If anyone has a right to know, it's Harry. If it wasn't for Harry...

135
00:14:08,690 --> 00:14:10,910
...we wouldn't even know voldemort was back.

136
00:14:10,920 --> 00:14:12,650
He's not a child, Molly.

137
00:14:12,660 --> 00:14:15,330
But he's not an adult either.

138
00:14:15,330 --> 00:14:18,420
-He's not James, Sirius. -Well, he's not your son.

139
00:14:18,430 --> 00:14:20,890
He's as good as.

140
00:14:20,970 --> 00:14:22,830
-Who else has he got? -Hey, Ginny.

141
00:14:22,840 --> 00:14:25,430
-He's got me. -How touchingly paternal, Black.

142
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:28,700
Perhaps Potter will grow up to be a felon, just like his godfather.

143
00:14:28,710 --> 00:14:30,630
Now, you stay out of this, Snivellus.

144
00:14:30,640 --> 00:14:32,870
-Snape's part of the order? -Git.

145
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:34,910
About your supposed reformation.

146
00:14:34,920 --> 00:14:37,810
-I know better. -So why don't you tell him?

147
00:14:37,820 --> 00:14:39,680
-Get off it. -Quick.

148
00:14:39,690 --> 00:14:41,610
-Get it up. -Crookshanks.

149
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:44,050
-Stop it. -Get off, you bloody cat.

150
00:14:44,060 --> 00:14:46,620
-Crookshanks. Leave it alone. -Get it up.

151
00:14:48,300 --> 00:14:52,260
-Hermione, I hate your cat. -Bad crookshanks.

152
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:56,160
Well, we'll be eating down in the kitchen.

153
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:59,300
Just because you're allowed to use magic now...

154
00:14:59,310 --> 00:15:02,500
...does not mean you have to whip your wands out for everything.

155
00:15:02,510 --> 00:15:04,400
Hi, Mum.

156
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:06,970
You hungry, Harry?

157
00:15:06,980 --> 00:15:09,770
You sure you're all right, Harry? Gave us quite a turn.

158
00:15:09,780 --> 00:15:12,240
Harry Potter.

159
00:15:14,150 --> 00:15:16,250
Sirius.

160
00:15:21,700 --> 00:15:24,120
This is very, very peculiar.

161
00:15:24,130 --> 00:15:26,010
It seems your hearing in the Ministry is

162
00:15:26,020 --> 00:15:27,960
to be before the entire wizengamot.

163
00:15:27,970 --> 00:15:31,700
I don't understand. What has the Ministry of Magic got against me?

164
00:15:32,340 --> 00:15:36,040
Show him. He'll find out soon enough.

165
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:49,450
He's been attacking Dumbledore as well.

166
00:15:50,990 --> 00:15:56,290
Fudge is using all his power, including his influence at the Daily Prophet...

167
00:15:56,300 --> 00:15:59,460
...to smear anyone who claims the Dark Lord has returned.

168
00:15:59,470 --> 00:16:00,920
Why?

169
00:16:00,930 --> 00:16:03,060
He thinks Dumbledore's after his job.

170
00:16:03,070 --> 00:16:05,360
No one in their right mind could believe that...

171
00:16:05,370 --> 00:16:08,400
Exactly the point. Fudge isn't in his right mind.

172
00:16:08,410 --> 00:16:11,230
It's been twisted and warped by fear.

173
00:16:12,610 --> 00:16:15,210
Now, fear makes people do terrible things, Harry.

174
00:16:15,220 --> 00:16:17,810
The last time Voldemort gained power...

175
00:16:17,820 --> 00:16:21,310
...he almost destroyed everything we hold most dear.

176
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:22,860
Now he's returned,

177
00:16:22,860 --> 00:16:25,420
and I'm afraid the minister will do almost anything...

178
00:16:25,430 --> 00:16:28,660
...to avoid facing that terrifying truth.

179
00:16:29,630 --> 00:16:34,590
We think Voldemort wants to build up his army again.

180
00:16:35,440 --> 00:16:38,260
Fourteen years ago, he had huge numbers at his command.

181
00:16:38,270 --> 00:16:43,130
And not just witches and wizards, but all manner of dark creatures.

182
00:16:43,440 --> 00:16:47,770
He's been recruiting heavily, and we've been attempting to do the same.

183
00:16:48,420 --> 00:16:52,480
But gathering followers isn't the only thing he's interested in.

184
00:16:55,120 --> 00:16:57,250
We believe...

185
00:16:57,930 --> 00:17:00,050
...Voldemort may be after something.

186
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:01,450
Sirius.

187
00:17:04,800 --> 00:17:07,970
Something he didn't have last time.

188
00:17:09,140 --> 00:17:11,330
You mean like a weapon?

189
00:17:11,340 --> 00:17:15,570
No. That's enough. He's just a boy.

190
00:17:15,580 --> 00:17:18,540
You say more and you might as well induct him into the order.

191
00:17:18,550 --> 00:17:19,970
Good. I want to join.

192
00:17:19,980 --> 00:17:22,420
If Voldemort's raising an army, then I want to fight.

193
00:17:34,830 --> 00:17:36,850
Harry.

194
00:17:36,860 --> 00:17:39,290
You are hereby expelled.

195
00:17:39,300 --> 00:17:42,400
Before the entire Wizengamot.

196
00:17:51,410 --> 00:17:53,370
Trains. Underground.

197
00:17:53,380 --> 00:17:55,980
Ingenious, these Muggles.

198
00:18:12,870 --> 00:18:15,000
Here we are.

199
00:18:16,500 --> 00:18:21,260
I've never used the visitors' entrance before. Should be fun.

200
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:26,310
Right. Good. I'll just get my Muggle money.

201
00:19:05,990 --> 00:19:09,080
Terrible. Lost a lot of Galleons trading on the potions market.

202
00:19:09,090 --> 00:19:12,550
Daily Prophet, ladies and gentlemen. Anybody for Daily Prophet?

203
00:19:12,560 --> 00:19:15,850
Dumbledore: Is he daft, or is he dangerous?

204
00:19:37,520 --> 00:19:40,620
-Morning, Arthur. -Morning, Bob.

205
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:44,680
Interdepartmental memos.

206
00:19:44,690 --> 00:19:48,950
We used to use owls. Mess was unbelievable.

207
00:19:53,800 --> 00:19:57,390
Merlin's beard. Thank you, Kingsley.

208
00:19:57,400 --> 00:20:01,070
-They've changed the time of your hearing. -When is it?

209
00:20:01,170 --> 00:20:03,340
In five minutes.

210
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:14,250
Department of Mysteries.

211
00:20:16,490 --> 00:20:20,780
And I'm confident, minister, that you will do the right thing.

212
00:20:20,790 --> 00:20:23,190
Yes, but we must be...

213
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:33,630
Remember, during the hearing, speak only when you're spoken to.

214
00:20:33,640 --> 00:20:37,470
Keep calm. You've done nothing wrong.

215
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:41,040
As the Muggles say, truth will out.

216
00:20:41,250 --> 00:20:42,910
Yes?

217
00:20:43,780 --> 00:20:46,380
I'm not allowed in, I'm afraid.

218
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:49,780
Good luck, Harry.

219
00:20:53,430 --> 00:20:56,120
Disciplinary hearing of the 12th of August...

220
00:20:56,130 --> 00:20:59,220
...into offenses committed by Harry James Potter...

221
00:20:59,230 --> 00:21:03,030
...resident at Number 4 Privet Drive, Little whinging, Surrey.

222
00:21:03,040 --> 00:21:03,580
Interrogators:

223
00:21:03,580 --> 00:21:06,300
Cornelius oswald Fudge, Minister of Mag...

224
00:21:06,310 --> 00:21:08,300
witness for the defense.

225
00:21:08,310 --> 00:21:11,770
Albus Percival wulfric...

226
00:21:11,810 --> 00:21:15,510
...Brian Dumbledore.

227
00:21:15,520 --> 00:21:18,940
You got our message that the time and place of the hearing...

228
00:21:18,950 --> 00:21:20,340
...had been changed, did you?

229
00:21:20,350 --> 00:21:21,680
I must have missed it.

230
00:21:21,690 --> 00:21:25,920
But by a happy mistake, I arrived at the Ministry three hours early.

231
00:21:28,600 --> 00:21:29,950
The charges?

232
00:21:29,960 --> 00:21:32,660
The charges against the accused are as follows:

233
00:21:32,670 --> 00:21:34,460
"That he did knowingly...

234
00:21:34,470 --> 00:21:38,200
...and in full awareness of the illegality of his actions...

235
00:21:38,210 --> 00:21:41,360
...produce a Patronus charm...

236
00:21:41,370 --> 00:21:44,770
...in the presence of a Muggle."

237
00:21:44,780 --> 00:21:48,240
-Do you deny producing said Patronus? -No, but...

238
00:21:48,250 --> 00:21:51,880
And you were aware that you were forbidden to use magic outside school...

239
00:21:51,890 --> 00:21:54,910
-...while under the age of 17? -Yes, I was, but...

240
00:21:54,920 --> 00:21:58,450
witches and wizards of the wizengamot...

241
00:21:58,460 --> 00:22:00,990
I was only doing it because of the Dementors.

242
00:22:03,430 --> 00:22:05,360
Dementors?

243
00:22:05,670 --> 00:22:07,520
In Little whinging?

244
00:22:07,530 --> 00:22:10,030
That's quite clever.

245
00:22:10,040 --> 00:22:13,430
Muggles can't see Dementors, can they, boy?

246
00:22:13,440 --> 00:22:15,730
-Highly convenient. -I'm not lying.

247
00:22:15,740 --> 00:22:18,470
-There were two of them, and if I hadn't... -Enough.

248
00:22:18,480 --> 00:22:19,570
I'm sorry to interrupt

249
00:22:19,570 --> 00:22:22,840
what I'm sure would have been a very well-rehearsed story...

250
00:22:22,850 --> 00:22:27,510
...but since you can produce no witnesses of the event...

251
00:22:27,520 --> 00:22:32,420
Pardon me, minister, but as it happens, we can.

252
00:22:35,460 --> 00:22:38,860
Please describe the attack.

253
00:22:41,330 --> 00:22:43,430
What did they look like?

254
00:22:43,700 --> 00:22:49,440
Well, one of them was very large and the other rather skinny.

255
00:22:50,240 --> 00:22:53,200
Not the boys. The Dementors.

256
00:22:53,210 --> 00:22:57,180
Oh, right, right. Well, big.

257
00:22:58,080 --> 00:23:02,980
Cloaked. Then everything went cold...

258
00:23:03,320 --> 00:23:06,880
...as though all the happiness had gone from the world.

259
00:23:06,890 --> 00:23:12,160
Now, look here. Dementors don't just wander into a Muggle suburb...

260
00:23:12,170 --> 00:23:15,960
...and happen across a wizard. The odds are astronomical.

261
00:23:15,970 --> 00:23:17,860
I don't think anyone would believe...

262
00:23:17,870 --> 00:23:21,200
...the Dementors were there by coincidence, minister.

263
00:23:23,440 --> 00:23:26,470
I'm sure I must have misunderstood you, professor.

264
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:32,140
Dementors are, after all, under the control of the Ministry of Magic.

265
00:23:32,150 --> 00:23:36,510
And it's so silly of me, but it sounded for a moment as though...

266
00:23:36,520 --> 00:23:40,680
...you were suggesting that the Ministry had ordered the attack on this boy.

267
00:23:40,690 --> 00:23:43,650
That would be disturbing indeed, Madam Undersecretary...

268
00:23:43,660 --> 00:23:47,990
...which is why I'm sure the Ministry will be mounting a full-scale inquiry...

269
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:49,620
...into why the two Dementors were

270
00:23:49,630 --> 00:23:51,530
so very far from Azkaban...

271
00:23:51,540 --> 00:23:55,210
...and why they mounted an attack without authorization.

272
00:23:55,780 --> 00:23:58,310
Of course, there is someone...

273
00:23:58,350 --> 00:24:01,240
...who might be behind the attack.

274
00:24:03,950 --> 00:24:08,750
Cornelius, I implore you to see reason.

275
00:24:08,760 --> 00:24:13,480
The evidence that the Dark Lord has returned is incontrovertible.

276
00:24:13,490 --> 00:24:16,560
He is not back.

277
00:24:22,170 --> 00:24:24,660
In the matter of Harry Potter...

278
00:24:24,940 --> 00:24:27,600
...the law clearly states...

279
00:24:27,610 --> 00:24:32,170
...that magic may be used before Muggles in life-threatening situations.

280
00:24:32,180 --> 00:24:35,240
Laws can be changed if necessary, Dumbledore.

281
00:24:35,250 --> 00:24:37,080
Clearly. Has it become practice to hold

282
00:24:37,090 --> 00:24:38,580
a full criminal trial...

283
00:24:38,590 --> 00:24:41,750
...to deal with a simple matter of underage magic?

284
00:24:49,860 --> 00:24:53,720
Those in favor of conviction?

285
00:25:02,240 --> 00:25:07,480
Those in favor of clearing the accused of all charges?

286
00:25:21,290 --> 00:25:23,860
Cleared of all charges.

287
00:25:26,600 --> 00:25:28,630
Professor.

288
00:25:41,280 --> 00:25:44,510
Padfoot. Are you barking mad?

289
00:25:44,520 --> 00:25:47,180
You'll blow the entire operation.

290
00:25:55,300 --> 00:25:58,090
Sirius, what are you doing here? If somebody sees you...

291
00:25:58,100 --> 00:26:00,990
I had to see you off, didn't I?

292
00:26:02,500 --> 00:26:05,200
What's life without a little risk?

293
00:26:05,210 --> 00:26:07,700
I don't wanna see you get chucked back in Azkaban.

294
00:26:07,710 --> 00:26:09,470
Don't worry about me.

295
00:26:09,610 --> 00:26:14,900
Anyway, I wanted you to have this.

296
00:26:19,990 --> 00:26:23,310
Original order of the Phoenix.

297
00:26:23,560 --> 00:26:25,450
Marlene McKinnon.

298
00:26:25,460 --> 00:26:28,320
She was killed two weeks after this was taken.

299
00:26:28,390 --> 00:26:31,860
Voldemort wiped out her entire family.

300
00:26:32,000 --> 00:26:33,960
Frank and Alice Longbottom.

301
00:26:33,970 --> 00:26:35,630
Neville's parents.

302
00:26:35,640 --> 00:26:39,600
They suffered a fate worse than death, you ask me.

303
00:26:41,240 --> 00:26:44,010
It's been 14 years.

304
00:26:44,540 --> 00:26:49,040
And still a day doesn't go by I don't miss your dad.

305
00:26:53,420 --> 00:26:56,380
Do you really think there's going to be a war, Sirius?

306
00:26:58,760 --> 00:27:02,080
It feels like it did before.

307
00:27:06,030 --> 00:27:08,130
You keep it.

308
00:27:08,300 --> 00:27:13,000
Anyway, I suppose you're the young ones now.

309
00:27:14,910 --> 00:27:16,900
I'll see you at the train.

310
00:27:16,910 --> 00:27:19,240
Bye-bye, darling.

311
00:27:19,850 --> 00:27:21,610
I love you.

312
00:27:22,080 --> 00:27:24,340
Hold my hand, lovey.

313
00:27:24,350 --> 00:27:26,780
There they are. They're in the far carriage.

314
00:27:26,790 --> 00:27:28,380
Bye.

315
00:28:10,300 --> 00:28:13,390
I'm surprised the Ministry's still letting you walk around free.

316
00:28:13,400 --> 00:28:15,020
Better enjoy it while you can.

317
00:28:15,030 --> 00:28:18,630
I expect there's a cell in Azkaban with your name on it.

318
00:28:20,940 --> 00:28:25,200
-What'd I tell you? Complete nutter. -Just stay away from me!

319
00:28:26,110 --> 00:28:28,240
It's only Malfoy.

320
00:28:28,780 --> 00:28:30,910
What'd you expect?

321
00:28:50,600 --> 00:28:51,930
Hi, guys.

322
00:28:51,940 --> 00:28:53,900
-Hey, Neville. -Hey there, Neville.

323
00:29:06,650 --> 00:29:08,480
What is it?

324
00:29:10,360 --> 00:29:13,920
-What's what? -That. Pulling the carriage.

325
00:29:14,460 --> 00:29:17,060
Nothing's pulling the carriage, Harry.

326
00:29:17,400 --> 00:29:19,930
It's pulling itself, like always.

327
00:29:33,250 --> 00:29:35,780
You're not going mad.

328
00:29:38,050 --> 00:29:40,580
I can see them too.

329
00:29:41,550 --> 00:29:44,450
You're just as sane as I am.

330
00:29:48,960 --> 00:29:51,320
Everyone, this is Loony Love...

331
00:29:53,830 --> 00:29:56,030
Luna Lovegood.

332
00:29:59,670 --> 00:30:02,300
What an interesting necklace.

333
00:30:02,540 --> 00:30:05,000
It's a charm, actually.

334
00:30:06,080 --> 00:30:07,970
Keeps away the Nargles.

335
00:30:11,450 --> 00:30:13,240
Hungry.

336
00:30:13,620 --> 00:30:15,890
I hope there's pudding.

337
00:30:16,590 --> 00:30:20,480
-What's a Nargle? -No idea.

338
00:30:32,910 --> 00:30:34,800
Good evening, children.

339
00:30:35,810 --> 00:30:38,700
Now, we have two changes in staffing this year.

340
00:30:38,710 --> 00:30:41,900
We're pleased to welcome back Professor Grubbly-Plank...

341
00:30:41,910 --> 00:30:44,640
...who'll be taking care of Magical creatures...

342
00:30:44,650 --> 00:30:48,410
...while Professor Hagrid is on temporary leave.

343
00:30:48,960 --> 00:30:53,120
We also wish to welcome our new Defense Against the Dark Arts teacher...

344
00:30:53,130 --> 00:30:56,590
...Professor Dolores Umbridge.

345
00:30:56,600 --> 00:31:00,630
And I'm sure you'll all join me in wishing the professor good luck.

346
00:31:01,130 --> 00:31:06,430
Now, as usual, our caretaker, Mr. Filch, has asked me to remind you...

347
00:31:17,220 --> 00:31:20,110
She was at my hearing. She works for Fudge.

348
00:31:20,120 --> 00:31:26,120
Thank you, headmaster, for those kind words of welcome.

349
00:31:27,190 --> 00:31:32,850
And how lovely to see all your bright...

350
00:31:32,860 --> 00:31:34,160
...happy faces smiling up at me.

351
00:31:34,230 --> 00:31:39,600
I'm sure we're all going to be very good friends.

352
00:31:39,610 --> 00:31:42,140
-That's likely. -That's likely.

353
00:31:44,680 --> 00:31:47,800
The Ministry of Magic has always considered...

354
00:31:47,810 --> 00:31:53,710
...the education of young witches and wizards to be of vital importance.

355
00:31:53,790 --> 00:31:56,210
Although each headmaster...

356
00:31:56,220 --> 00:32:01,360
...has brought something new to this historic school...

357
00:32:02,630 --> 00:32:09,060
...progress for the sake of progress must be discouraged.

358
00:32:09,500 --> 00:32:13,500
Let us preserve what must be preserved...

359
00:32:13,510 --> 00:32:17,170
...perfect what can be perfected...

360
00:32:17,180 --> 00:32:24,080
...and prune practices that ought to be prohibited.

361
00:32:30,860 --> 00:32:35,120
Thank you, Professor Umbridge. That really was most illuminating.

362
00:32:35,130 --> 00:32:39,800
-Illuminating? What a load of waffle. -What's it mean?

363
00:32:40,230 --> 00:32:42,560
Magic is forbidden in the corridors...

364
00:32:42,570 --> 00:32:46,430
It means the Ministry's interfering at Hogwarts.

365
00:33:05,930 --> 00:33:07,950
Dean, Seamus.

366
00:33:07,960 --> 00:33:10,390
-Good holiday? -All right.

367
00:33:10,460 --> 00:33:12,990
Better than Seamus', anyway.

368
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:16,490
Me mum didn't want me to come back this year.

369
00:33:16,500 --> 00:33:20,100
-Why not? -Let me see. Because of you.

370
00:33:20,240 --> 00:33:23,770
The Daily Prophet's been saying a lot of things about you and Dumbledore.

371
00:33:23,780 --> 00:33:25,270
What, your mum believes them?

372
00:33:25,280 --> 00:33:27,340
Nobody was there the night cedric died.

373
00:33:27,350 --> 00:33:30,610
I guess you should read the Prophet, then, like your stupid mother.

374
00:33:30,620 --> 00:33:32,340
Don't talk about my mother.

375
00:33:32,350 --> 00:33:34,280
I'll have a go at anyone that calls me a liar.

376
00:33:34,290 --> 00:33:36,950
-What's going on? -He's mad, is what's going on.

377
00:33:36,960 --> 00:33:40,220
Do you believe the rubbish he's come out with about You-Know-who?

378
00:33:40,230 --> 00:33:42,150
Yeah. I do.

379
00:33:42,900 --> 00:33:45,130
Has anyone else got a problem with Harry?

380
00:33:54,270 --> 00:33:56,830
-You all right? -Fine.

381
00:33:56,840 --> 00:33:59,940
Seamus was bang out of order, mate.

382
00:34:00,210 --> 00:34:01,960
But he'll come through, you'll see.

383
00:34:01,970 --> 00:34:03,730
I said, I'm fine, Ron.

384
00:34:07,650 --> 00:34:12,360
Right. I'll just leave you to your thoughts, then.

385
00:34:40,520 --> 00:34:41,810
Harry.

386
00:34:56,970 --> 00:34:59,430
Bring it over here. Over here.

387
00:35:00,040 --> 00:35:03,210
Oh, go on, Seamus. Go on, get it.

388
00:35:18,560 --> 00:35:20,260
Good morning, children.

389
00:35:21,990 --> 00:35:27,290
Ordinary wizarding Level examinations.

390
00:35:27,300 --> 00:35:30,060
O-W-Ls.

391
00:35:30,070 --> 00:35:34,800
More commonly known as owLs.

392
00:35:34,810 --> 00:35:38,240
Study hard and you will be rewarded.

393
00:35:38,280 --> 00:35:43,840
Fail to do so, and the consequences may be severe.

394
00:35:49,120 --> 00:35:54,350
Your previous instruction in this subject has been disturbingly uneven.

395
00:35:54,360 --> 00:35:56,650
But you'll be pleased to know, from now on...

396
00:35:56,660 --> 00:36:00,320
...you will be following a carefully structured, Ministry-approved...

397
00:36:00,330 --> 00:36:03,330
...course of defensive magic. Yes?

398
00:36:04,370 --> 00:36:07,130
There's nothing in here about using defensive spells?

399
00:36:07,140 --> 00:36:08,830
Using spells?

400
00:36:08,840 --> 00:36:12,600
Well, I can't imagine why you would need to use spells in my classroom.

401
00:36:14,010 --> 00:36:15,770
We're not gonna use magic?

402
00:36:15,780 --> 00:36:20,940
You'll be learning about defensive spells in a secure, risk-free way.

403
00:36:20,950 --> 00:36:23,880
What use is that? If we're attacked, it won't be risk-free.

404
00:36:23,890 --> 00:36:27,120
Students will raise their hands when they speak in my class.

405
00:36:30,460 --> 00:36:33,020
It is the view of the Ministry...

406
00:36:33,030 --> 00:36:35,960
...that a theoretical knowledge will be sufficient...

407
00:36:35,970 --> 00:36:38,090
...to get you through your examinations...

408
00:36:38,100 --> 00:36:40,700
...which, after all, is what school is all about.

409
00:36:40,710 --> 00:36:43,670
And how's theory supposed to prepare us for what's out there?

410
00:36:43,680 --> 00:36:45,870
There is nothing out there, dear.

411
00:36:45,880 --> 00:36:49,070
Who do you imagine wants to attack children like yourself?

412
00:36:49,080 --> 00:36:52,650
Oh, I don't know. Maybe Lord Voldemort.

413
00:37:03,030 --> 00:37:07,820
Now, let me make this quite plain.

414
00:37:08,070 --> 00:37:09,690
You have been told...

415
00:37:09,700 --> 00:37:15,230
...that a certain dark wizard is at large once again.

416
00:37:15,240 --> 00:37:16,780
-This is a lie.

417
00:37:16,780 --> 00:37:20,540
-It's not a lie. I saw him. I fought him.

418
00:37:20,550 --> 00:37:22,340
Detention, Mr. Potter.

419
00:37:22,350 --> 00:37:24,670
Cedric Diggory dropped dead of his own accord?

420
00:37:24,680 --> 00:37:27,280
Cedric Diggory's death was a tragic accident.

421
00:37:27,290 --> 00:37:29,180
It was murder. Voldemort killed him.

422
00:37:29,190 --> 00:37:31,390
-You must know that! -Enough!

423
00:37:31,760 --> 00:37:33,620
Enough.

424
00:37:33,630 --> 00:37:38,230
See me later, Mr. Potter. My office.

425
00:38:02,690 --> 00:38:04,180
Come in.

426
00:38:09,130 --> 00:38:11,360
Good evening, Mr. Potter.

427
00:38:11,700 --> 00:38:13,260
Sit.

428
00:38:20,670 --> 00:38:24,730
You're going to be doing some lines for me today, Mr. Potter.

429
00:38:24,740 --> 00:38:26,840
No, not with your quill.

430
00:38:26,850 --> 00:38:30,340
Going to be using a rather special one of mine.

431
00:38:35,190 --> 00:38:36,890
Now...

432
00:38:37,560 --> 00:38:43,730
...I want you to write, "I must not tell lies."

433
00:38:45,500 --> 00:38:47,700
How many times?

434
00:38:47,830 --> 00:38:52,800
Well, let's say for as long as it takes for the message to sink in.

435
00:38:54,510 --> 00:38:56,330
You haven't given me any ink.

436
00:38:56,340 --> 00:38:58,130
Oh, you won't need any ink.

437
00:39:49,090 --> 00:39:50,880
Yes?

438
00:39:57,900 --> 00:40:01,600
-Nothing. -That's right.

439
00:40:02,210 --> 00:40:06,340
Because you know, deep down...

440
00:40:06,350 --> 00:40:08,700
...you deserve to be punished.

441
00:40:09,580 --> 00:40:12,040
Don't you, Mr. Potter?

442
00:40:15,990 --> 00:40:17,880
Go on.

443
00:40:26,630 --> 00:40:29,060
-Skiving Snackboxes. -Sweets that make you ill.

444
00:40:29,070 --> 00:40:30,860
Get out of class whenever you like.

445
00:40:30,870 --> 00:40:34,940
Obtain hours of pleasure from unprofitable boredom.

446
00:40:35,640 --> 00:40:37,130
Care for another?

447
00:40:37,140 --> 00:40:39,840
-I'm not asking you to write all of it for me. -Please.

448
00:40:39,850 --> 00:40:43,110
I've been busy studying for these stupid owL exams.

449
00:40:43,280 --> 00:40:45,240
I'll do the introduction. That's all.

450
00:40:45,250 --> 00:40:49,180
Hermione, you're honestly the most wonderful person I've ever met.

451
00:40:49,190 --> 00:40:53,720
-And if I'm ever rude to you again... -I'll know you've gone back to normal.

452
00:40:58,460 --> 00:41:00,860
What's wrong with your hand?

453
00:41:01,100 --> 00:41:02,870
Nothing.

454
00:41:03,840 --> 00:41:06,040
The other hand.

455
00:41:08,240 --> 00:41:10,230
-You've got to tell Dumbledore. -No.

456
00:41:10,240 --> 00:41:12,600
Dumbledore's got enough on his mind right now.

457
00:41:12,610 --> 00:41:14,900
I don't want to give Umbridge the satisfaction.

458
00:41:14,910 --> 00:41:17,510
Bloody hell, Harry. The woman's torturing you.

459
00:41:17,520 --> 00:41:21,750
-If the parents knew about this... -I haven't got any of those, have I, Ron?

460
00:41:24,260 --> 00:41:26,880
Harry, you've got to report this.

461
00:41:26,890 --> 00:41:30,590
-It's perfectly simple. You're being... -No, it's not.

462
00:41:30,600 --> 00:41:33,730
Hermione, whatever this is, it's not simple.

463
00:41:34,470 --> 00:41:36,790
You don't understand.

464
00:41:39,100 --> 00:41:41,340
Then help us to.

465
00:41:55,750 --> 00:41:57,920
Dear Padfoot...

466
00:41:58,160 --> 00:42:00,050
...I hope you're all right.

467
00:42:00,060 --> 00:42:04,960
It's starting to get colder here. Winter is definitely on the way.

468
00:42:07,300 --> 00:42:12,330
In spite of being back at Hogwarts, I feel more alone than ever.

469
00:42:12,910 --> 00:42:16,500
I know you, of all people, will understand.

470
00:42:50,310 --> 00:42:52,800
Hello, Harry Potter.

471
00:42:55,150 --> 00:43:00,080
-Your feet. Aren't they cold? -Bit.

472
00:43:00,690 --> 00:43:05,010
Unfortunately, all my shoes have mysteriously disappeared.

473
00:43:05,290 --> 00:43:08,650
I suspect Nargles are behind it.

474
00:43:14,700 --> 00:43:18,630
-What are they? -They're called Thestrals.

475
00:43:19,000 --> 00:43:20,500
They're quite gentle, really,

476
00:43:20,500 --> 00:43:24,370
but people avoid them because they're a bit...

477
00:43:27,010 --> 00:43:28,940
Different.

478
00:43:31,750 --> 00:43:34,280
But why can't the others see them?

479
00:43:34,290 --> 00:43:38,110
They can only be seen by people who've seen death.

480
00:43:39,930 --> 00:43:42,720
So you've known someone who's died, then?

481
00:43:42,730 --> 00:43:44,660
My mum.

482
00:43:44,900 --> 00:43:49,960
She was quite an extraordinary witch, but she did like to experiment...

483
00:43:49,970 --> 00:43:53,430
...and one day, one of her spells went badly wrong.

484
00:43:53,440 --> 00:43:56,140
-I was 9. -I'm sorry.

485
00:43:56,410 --> 00:43:58,770
Yes, it was rather horrible.

486
00:43:58,780 --> 00:44:04,410
I do feel very sad about it sometimes, but I've got Dad.

487
00:44:06,350 --> 00:44:09,280
We both believe you, by the way.

488
00:44:12,060 --> 00:44:15,220
That He-who-Must-Not-Be-Named is back, and you fought him...

489
00:44:15,230 --> 00:44:18,490
...and the Ministry and the Prophet are conspiring against you.

490
00:44:18,500 --> 00:44:23,030
Thanks. It seems you're about the only ones that do.

491
00:44:23,040 --> 00:44:24,670
I don't think that's true.

492
00:44:26,740 --> 00:44:30,030
But I suppose that's how he wants you to feel.

493
00:44:30,040 --> 00:44:32,110
What do you mean?

494
00:44:32,440 --> 00:44:34,610
Well, if I were You-Know-who...

495
00:44:34,780 --> 00:44:38,510
...l'd want you to feel cut off from everyone else...

496
00:44:38,520 --> 00:44:41,550
...because if it's just you alone...

497
00:44:42,090 --> 00:44:44,720
...you're not as much of a threat.

498
00:45:02,070 --> 00:45:07,110
-Do you ever stop eating?  -What? I'm hungry.

499
00:45:10,180 --> 00:45:11,540
Harry.

500
00:45:13,090 --> 00:45:14,610
Can I join you?

501
00:45:16,220 --> 00:45:19,510
Pardon me, professor, but what exactly are you insinuating?

502
00:45:19,520 --> 00:45:22,450
I am merely requesting that when it comes to my students...

503
00:45:22,460 --> 00:45:26,890
...you conform to the prescribed disciplinary practices.

504
00:45:26,900 --> 00:45:28,720
So silly of me, but it sounds...

505
00:45:28,730 --> 00:45:33,030
...as if you're questioning my authority in my own classroom...

506
00:45:33,040 --> 00:45:34,530
...Minerva.

507
00:45:34,540 --> 00:45:39,270
Not at all, Dolores, merely your medieval methods.

508
00:45:39,280 --> 00:45:41,900
I am sorry, dear.

509
00:45:41,910 --> 00:45:45,410
But to question my practices is to question the Ministry...

510
00:45:45,420 --> 00:45:48,710
...and by extension, the minister himself.

511
00:45:48,720 --> 00:45:50,480
I am a tolerant woman...

512
00:45:50,490 --> 00:45:55,850
...but the one thing I will not stand for is disloyalty.

513
00:45:57,330 --> 00:45:59,390
Disloyalty.

514
00:46:00,830 --> 00:46:04,960
Things at Hogwarts are far worse than I feared.

515
00:46:04,970 --> 00:46:08,730
Cornelius will want to take immediate action.

516
00:46:19,850 --> 00:46:21,910
What's happened to Dumbledore?

517
00:46:21,920 --> 00:46:27,780
Having already revolutionized  the teaching of Defense Against the Dark Arts

518
00:46:27,990 --> 00:46:32,750
...Dolores Umbridge will, as high inquisitor, have powers...

519
00:46:32,970 --> 00:46:39,430
...to address the seriously falling standards at Hogwarts School.

520
00:46:46,910 --> 00:46:49,240
Just one question, dear.

521
00:46:49,250 --> 00:46:53,750
You've been in this post how long, exactly?

522
00:47:00,260 --> 00:47:05,520
You applied first for the Defense Against the Dark Arts post, is that correct?

523
00:47:05,530 --> 00:47:07,820
Yes.

524
00:47:07,930 --> 00:47:10,860
But you were unsuccessful?

525
00:47:11,770 --> 00:47:14,500
Obviously.

526
00:47:46,540 --> 00:47:50,270
Could you please predict something for me?

527
00:47:51,710 --> 00:47:53,200
I'm sorry?

528
00:47:58,150 --> 00:48:00,650
Move those mouths.

529
00:48:06,490 --> 00:48:09,890
One teensy little prophecy?

530
00:48:15,470 --> 00:48:17,200
Pity.

531
00:48:17,470 --> 00:48:20,030
No, wait. Wait, no. I think I do see something.

532
00:48:20,040 --> 00:48:22,500
Yes, I do. Something dark.

533
00:48:22,510 --> 00:48:27,340
You are in grave danger.

534
00:48:28,510 --> 00:48:30,540
Lovely.

535
00:48:40,430 --> 00:48:42,750
Cho. What's going on?

536
00:48:42,760 --> 00:48:45,390
It's Professor Trelawney.

537
00:49:14,930 --> 00:49:18,590
Sixteen years I've lived and taught here.

538
00:49:18,600 --> 00:49:21,830
Hogwarts is my home.

539
00:49:23,440 --> 00:49:25,640
You can't do this.

540
00:49:26,770 --> 00:49:29,340
Actually, I can.

541
00:49:37,920 --> 00:49:39,440
Something you'd like to say?

542
00:49:39,450 --> 00:49:42,410
Oh, there are several things I would like to say.

543
00:49:42,690 --> 00:49:44,550
There...

544
00:49:58,170 --> 00:50:03,130
Professor McGonagall, might I ask you to escort Sybil back inside?

545
00:50:04,140 --> 00:50:06,770
Sybil, dear. This way.

546
00:50:06,780 --> 00:50:08,570
Thank you.

547
00:50:09,450 --> 00:50:13,640
Dumbledore, may I remind you that under the terms...

548
00:50:13,650 --> 00:50:17,080
...of Educational Decree Number 23, as enacted by the minister...

549
00:50:17,090 --> 00:50:20,420
You have the right to dismiss my teachers.

550
00:50:20,430 --> 00:50:24,150
You do not, however, have the authority to banish them from the grounds.

551
00:50:24,160 --> 00:50:27,490
That power remains with the headmaster.

552
00:50:29,200 --> 00:50:30,760
For now.

553
00:50:36,910 --> 00:50:39,070
Don't you all have studying to do?

554
00:50:39,080 --> 00:50:40,540
Professor.

555
00:50:42,080 --> 00:50:43,470
Professor?

556
00:50:43,650 --> 00:50:46,610
Professor Dumbledore. Professor!

557
00:50:46,620 --> 00:50:49,050
Professor Dumbledore.

558
00:50:59,430 --> 00:51:01,820
That foul, evil, old gargoyle.

559
00:51:02,070 --> 00:51:04,840
We're not learning how to defend ourselves.

560
00:51:04,840 --> 00:51:07,400
We're not learning how to pass our owLs.

561
00:51:07,470 --> 00:51:09,660
She's taking over the entire school.

562
00:51:09,670 --> 00:51:14,500
Security has been and will remain the Ministry's top priority.

563
00:51:14,510 --> 00:51:17,510
Furthermore, we have convincing evidence...

564
00:51:17,520 --> 00:51:20,540
...that these disappearances are the work...

565
00:51:20,550 --> 00:51:24,250
...of notorious mass murderer Sirius Black.

566
00:51:24,690 --> 00:51:26,480
Harry.

567
00:51:26,490 --> 00:51:28,490
Sirius.

568
00:51:28,930 --> 00:51:31,790
-What are you doing here? -Answering your letter.

569
00:51:31,800 --> 00:51:34,860
You said you were worried about Umbridge. What's she doing?

570
00:51:34,870 --> 00:51:36,960
Training you to kill half-breeds?

571
00:51:36,970 --> 00:51:40,240
-She's not letting us use magic at all. -Well, I'm not surprised.

572
00:51:40,310 --> 00:51:44,530
The latest intelligence is that Fudge doesn't want you trained in combat.

573
00:51:44,540 --> 00:51:45,830
Combat?

574
00:51:46,040 --> 00:51:49,100
What does he think, we're forming some sort of wizard army?

575
00:51:49,110 --> 00:51:50,670
That's exactly what he thinks.

576
00:51:50,680 --> 00:51:54,920
That Dumbledore is assembling his own forces to take on the Ministry.

577
00:51:55,150 --> 00:51:58,750
He's becoming more paranoid by the minute.

578
00:51:58,820 --> 00:52:02,580
The others wouldn't want me telling you this, Harry...

579
00:52:02,830 --> 00:52:05,820
...but things aren't going at all well with the order.

580
00:52:05,830 --> 00:52:08,620
Fudge is blocking the truth at every turn...

581
00:52:08,630 --> 00:52:12,930
...and these disappearances are just how it started before.

582
00:52:13,440 --> 00:52:17,070
Voldemort is on the move.

583
00:52:17,180 --> 00:52:18,870
Well, what can we do?

584
00:52:19,180 --> 00:52:20,770
Someone's coming.

585
00:52:20,780 --> 00:52:23,140
I'm sorry I can't be of more help.

586
00:52:23,150 --> 00:52:28,440
But for now, at least, it looks like you're on your own.

587
00:52:39,700 --> 00:52:42,330
He really is out there, isn't he?

588
00:52:43,870 --> 00:52:46,830
We've got to be able to defend ourselves.

589
00:52:47,110 --> 00:52:51,170
And if Umbridge refuses to teach us how, we need someone who will.

590
00:53:07,890 --> 00:53:10,350
Harry.

591
00:53:19,640 --> 00:53:22,160
This is mad. Who'd wanna be taught by me?

592
00:53:22,170 --> 00:53:23,570
I'm a nutter, remember?

593
00:53:23,580 --> 00:53:28,300
Look on the bright side: You can't be any worse than old toad face.

594
00:53:28,310 --> 00:53:32,070
-Thanks, Ron. -I'm here for you, mate.

595
00:53:32,280 --> 00:53:34,780
Who's supposed to be meeting us, then?

596
00:53:34,790 --> 00:53:37,210
Just a couple of people.

597
00:53:41,930 --> 00:53:43,660
Lovely spot.

598
00:53:47,070 --> 00:53:49,360
Thought it would be safer off the beaten track.

599
00:53:49,370 --> 00:53:51,830
Matey, come back here.

600
00:54:01,550 --> 00:54:04,610
So you all know why we're here.

601
00:54:04,620 --> 00:54:06,140
We need a teacher.

602
00:54:07,550 --> 00:54:10,010
A proper teacher.

603
00:54:10,020 --> 00:54:13,350
One who's had experience defending themselves against the Dark Arts.

604
00:54:13,360 --> 00:54:15,280
-Why? -Why?

605
00:54:15,290 --> 00:54:17,520
Because You-Know-who's back, you tosspot.

606
00:54:17,530 --> 00:54:19,250
-So he says. -So Dumbledore says.

607
00:54:19,260 --> 00:54:21,560
So Dumbledore says because he says.

608
00:54:21,570 --> 00:54:24,270
The point is, where's the proof?

609
00:54:25,340 --> 00:54:28,660
If Potter could tell us more about how Diggory got killed...

610
00:54:31,480 --> 00:54:33,030
I'm not gonna talk about cedric

611
00:54:33,040 --> 00:54:35,400
so if that's why you're here, clear out now.

612
00:54:35,410 --> 00:54:36,440
Come on, Hermione. Let's go.

613
00:54:36,450 --> 00:54:39,010
-They're here because they think I'm some sort of freak. -Wait.

614
00:54:39,020 --> 00:54:41,950
Is it true you can produce a Patronus charm?

615
00:54:44,960 --> 00:54:46,690
Yes.

616
00:54:47,860 --> 00:54:49,450
I've seen it.

617
00:54:49,460 --> 00:54:51,890
Blimey, Harry. I didn't know you could do that.

618
00:54:52,260 --> 00:54:56,560
And he killed a basilisk, with the sword in Dumbledore's office.

619
00:54:56,570 --> 00:54:57,960
It's true.

620
00:54:57,970 --> 00:55:01,030
Third year, he fought off about a hundred Dementors at once.

621
00:55:02,040 --> 00:55:05,000
Last year, he really did fight off You-Know-who in the flesh.

622
00:55:05,010 --> 00:55:06,610
Wait.

623
00:55:07,010 --> 00:55:11,710
Look, it all sounds great when you say it like that...

624
00:55:11,720 --> 00:55:15,540
...but the truth is, most of that was just luck.

625
00:55:15,550 --> 00:55:17,220
I didn't know what I was doing half the time.

626
00:55:17,230 --> 00:55:19,070
I nearly always had help.

627
00:55:19,460 --> 00:55:23,250
-He's just being modest. -No, Hermione, I'm not.

628
00:55:25,530 --> 00:55:30,490
Facing this stuff in real life is not like school.

629
00:55:31,240 --> 00:55:34,830
In school, if you make a mistake, you can just try again tomorrow.

630
00:55:34,840 --> 00:55:36,630
But out there...

631
00:55:36,940 --> 00:55:40,400
...when you're a second away from being murdered...

632
00:55:40,410 --> 00:55:44,410
...or watching a friend die right before your eyes...

633
00:55:46,890 --> 00:55:48,980
You don't know what that's like.

634
00:55:58,460 --> 00:56:00,660
You're right, Harry, we don't.

635
00:56:01,130 --> 00:56:03,390
That's why we need your help.

636
00:56:03,400 --> 00:56:06,600
Because if we're going to have any chance at beating...

637
00:56:08,510 --> 00:56:09,970
...Voldemort...

638
00:56:13,110 --> 00:56:15,140
He's really back.

639
00:56:37,170 --> 00:56:38,990
Right. First we need to find a place to practice...

640
00:56:39,000 --> 00:56:40,560
...where Umbridge won't find out.

641
00:56:40,570 --> 00:56:42,900
-The Shrieking Shack. -It's too small.

642
00:56:42,910 --> 00:56:46,030
-Forbidden Forest? -Not bloody likely.

643
00:56:46,040 --> 00:56:48,300
Harry, what happens if Umbridge does find out?

644
00:56:48,310 --> 00:56:49,770
Who cares?

645
00:56:50,080 --> 00:56:55,110
I mean, it's sort of exciting, isn't it, breaking the rules?

646
00:56:55,120 --> 00:56:57,680
Who are you and what have you done with Hermione?

647
00:56:58,090 --> 00:57:01,920
Anyway, at least we know one positive thing that came from today.

648
00:57:01,930 --> 00:57:03,520
What's that?

649
00:57:04,960 --> 00:57:07,930
Cho couldn't take her eyes off you, could she?

650
00:57:10,370 --> 00:57:13,590
Right. Over the next few days, we should each come up...

651
00:57:13,600 --> 00:57:16,600
...with a couple of possibilities of places we can practice.

652
00:57:16,610 --> 00:57:20,600
We've got to make sure, wherever it is, there's no chance she can find us.

653
00:57:20,610 --> 00:57:22,740
Will do, Harry.

654
00:57:31,190 --> 00:57:35,480
All student organizations are henceforth disbanded.

655
00:57:35,490 --> 00:57:39,290
Any student in noncompliance will be expelled.

656
00:57:39,300 --> 00:57:42,070
Watch where you're going, Longbottom.

657
00:58:17,470 --> 00:58:21,900
You've done it, Neville. You found the Room of Requirement.

658
00:58:21,910 --> 00:58:23,200
The what?

659
00:58:23,210 --> 00:58:25,770
It's also known as the come and Go Room.

660
00:58:25,780 --> 00:58:29,370
The Room of Requirement only appears when a person has real need of it.

661
00:58:29,380 --> 00:58:32,210
And it's always equipped for the seeker's needs.

662
00:58:32,220 --> 00:58:36,250
So say you really needed the toilet...

663
00:58:37,120 --> 00:58:42,120
charming, Ronald. But, yes, that is the general idea.

664
00:58:42,130 --> 00:58:47,300
It's brilliant. It's like Hogwarts wants us to fight back.

665
00:58:58,040 --> 00:58:59,830
Expelliarmus.

666
00:59:04,680 --> 00:59:06,240
I'm hopeless.

667
00:59:06,250 --> 00:59:10,320
You're just flourishing your wand too much. Try it like this. Expelliarmus.

668
00:59:13,390 --> 00:59:17,590
You will please copy the approved text four times...

669
00:59:17,600 --> 00:59:20,890
...to ensure maximum retention.

670
00:59:20,970 --> 00:59:24,830
-There will be no need to talk. -No need to think's more like it.

671
00:59:24,840 --> 00:59:27,160
-Expelliarmus. -Wands away.

672
00:59:39,820 --> 00:59:43,040
Stunning is one of the most useful spells in your arsenal.

673
00:59:43,050 --> 00:59:45,450
It's a wizard's bread and butter, really.

674
00:59:45,460 --> 00:59:49,320
So come on, then, Nigel. Give it your best shot.

675
00:59:55,530 --> 00:59:57,230
Stupefy!

676
01:00:01,840 --> 01:00:06,580
Good. Not bad at all, Nigel. Well done.

677
01:00:11,650 --> 01:00:14,040
Don't worry. I'll go easy on you.

678
01:00:14,120 --> 01:00:16,410
Thanks, Ronald.

679
01:00:18,790 --> 01:00:21,150
-Come on, Ron. -Come on, Ron.

680
01:00:21,160 --> 01:00:24,330
-You can do it. -Come on, Ron.

681
01:00:24,560 --> 01:00:26,890
-One Sickle. -You're on.

682
01:00:33,640 --> 01:00:35,300
Stupefy.

683
01:00:40,680 --> 01:00:42,950
-Thank you. -Shut up.

684
01:00:43,050 --> 01:00:47,940
I let her do that. It's good manners, isn't it?

685
01:00:49,890 --> 01:00:52,710
It was completely intentional.

686
01:01:18,050 --> 01:01:21,280
Up you come. Would you like a cup of tea?

687
01:01:23,290 --> 01:01:27,550
Now, focus on a fixed point and try again.

688
01:01:27,830 --> 01:01:30,090
Expelliarmus.

689
01:01:31,360 --> 01:01:34,220
Very good. Keep your concentration.

690
01:01:36,030 --> 01:01:37,820
Great.

691
01:01:38,800 --> 01:01:40,700
A little higher.

692
01:01:48,880 --> 01:01:52,010
I'm okay. I'm okay.

693
01:02:09,730 --> 01:02:12,660
-Stupefy. -Stupefy.

694
01:02:13,940 --> 01:02:17,470
Those wishing to join the Inquisitorial Squad for extra credit...

695
01:02:17,480 --> 01:02:20,500
...may sign up in the high inquisitor's office.

696
01:02:20,510 --> 01:02:22,440
Diminuendo.

697
01:02:28,050 --> 01:02:32,510
Working hard is important, but there's something that matters even more:

698
01:02:32,520 --> 01:02:34,880
Believing in yourself.

699
01:02:34,890 --> 01:02:37,180
-Expelliarmus. -Levicorpus. Got it.

700
01:02:37,190 --> 01:02:38,920
Think of it this way.

701
01:02:38,930 --> 01:02:43,220
Every great wizard in history has started out...

702
01:02:43,270 --> 01:02:47,330
...as nothing more than what we are now: Students.

703
01:02:47,340 --> 01:02:50,570
If they can do it, why not us?

704
01:03:00,420 --> 01:03:02,520
-Stupefy. -Expelliarmus.

705
01:03:04,390 --> 01:03:06,050
Expelliarmus.

706
01:03:08,460 --> 01:03:10,250
Expelliarmus.

707
01:03:15,500 --> 01:03:17,100
Reducto.

708
01:03:30,310 --> 01:03:33,470
-Expelliarmus. -Expelliarmus.

709
01:03:33,480 --> 01:03:36,150
Expelliarmus.

710
01:03:39,760 --> 01:03:42,120
Expelliarmus.

711
01:03:45,660 --> 01:03:49,360
Fantastic, Neville. Well done, man.

712
01:03:50,700 --> 01:03:52,990
So that's it for this lesson.

713
01:03:53,000 --> 01:03:56,700
Now, we're not gonna be meeting again until after the holidays.

714
01:03:56,810 --> 01:04:00,000
So just keep practicing on your own as best you can.

715
01:04:00,010 --> 01:04:03,680
And well done, everyone. Great, great work.

716
01:04:08,190 --> 01:04:09,780
Well done, mate.

717
01:04:09,790 --> 01:04:11,520
Thanks.

718
01:04:16,890 --> 01:04:19,560
See you after christmas.

719
01:04:28,710 --> 01:04:31,070
See you in the common Room, Harry.

720
01:04:32,180 --> 01:04:35,170
-Thanks a lot, Harry. -No worries.

721
01:04:36,650 --> 01:04:39,310
-Thank you so much. -Not at all. Merry christmas.

722
01:04:39,480 --> 01:04:42,010
-Thank you, Harry. -Thank you. Merry christmas.

723
01:04:42,020 --> 01:04:44,040
-Merry christmas. -Have a good christmas.

724
01:04:44,050 --> 01:04:46,810
-Have a great christmas, Luna. -We've been thinking.

725
01:04:46,820 --> 01:04:49,380
We could always slip Umbridge some Puking Pastilles.

726
01:04:49,390 --> 01:04:52,220
Or Fever Fudge. They give you massive, pus-filled boils...

727
01:04:52,230 --> 01:04:55,050
Sounds great, guys. Would you excuse me?

728
01:05:05,710 --> 01:05:10,600
Are you all right? I heard Umbridge gave you a rough time the other day.

729
01:05:10,610 --> 01:05:13,280
Yeah. I'm okay.

730
01:05:13,680 --> 01:05:16,780
Anyway, it's worth it.

731
01:05:21,830 --> 01:05:24,730
It's just, learning all this...

732
01:05:25,430 --> 01:05:29,020
...makes me wonder whether, if he'd known it...

733
01:05:29,030 --> 01:05:32,060
cedric did know this stuff.

734
01:05:33,000 --> 01:05:35,700
He was really good.

735
01:05:36,030 --> 01:05:39,060
It's just, Voldemort was better.

736
01:05:43,310 --> 01:05:45,400
You're a really good teacher, Harry.

737
01:05:46,380 --> 01:05:49,580
I've never been able to stun anything before.

738
01:05:58,420 --> 01:06:00,380
Mistletoe.

739
01:06:03,590 --> 01:06:05,830
Probably full of Nargles, though.

740
01:06:06,600 --> 01:06:08,590
What are Nargles?

741
01:06:09,000 --> 01:06:11,030
No idea.

742
01:06:32,760 --> 01:06:35,250
Well, how was it?

743
01:06:35,720 --> 01:06:37,790
Wet.

744
01:06:37,890 --> 01:06:39,960
I mean, she was sort of crying.

745
01:06:40,030 --> 01:06:42,150
That bad at it, are you?

746
01:06:42,160 --> 01:06:45,190
I'm sure Harry's kissing was more than satisfactory.

747
01:06:47,740 --> 01:06:50,060
Cho spends half her time crying these days.

748
01:06:50,070 --> 01:06:52,640
You'd think a bit of snogging would cheer her up.

749
01:06:53,810 --> 01:06:56,980
Don't you understand how she must be feeling?

750
01:07:01,080 --> 01:07:04,710
Well, obviously she's feeling sad about cedric...

751
01:07:04,720 --> 01:07:06,590
...and confused about liking Harry

752
01:07:06,600 --> 01:07:07,950
and guilty about kissing him...

753
01:07:07,960 --> 01:07:09,730
...conflicted because Umbridge

754
01:07:09,740 --> 01:07:11,350
might sack her mum from the Ministry...

755
01:07:11,360 --> 01:07:12,760
...and frightened of failing her owLs

756
01:07:12,770 --> 01:07:14,900
because she's worrying about everything.

757
01:07:17,030 --> 01:07:20,760
One person couldn't feel all that. They'd explode.

758
01:07:20,770 --> 01:07:24,300
Just because you've got the emotional range of a teaspoon...

759
01:07:39,850 --> 01:07:41,780
Harry.

760
01:07:50,260 --> 01:07:53,620
Voldemort may be after something.

761
01:07:54,000 --> 01:07:57,290
Something he didn't have last time.

762
01:07:57,840 --> 01:07:59,400
Harry.

763
01:08:00,740 --> 01:08:02,300
Harry.

764
01:08:33,110 --> 01:08:36,670
In the dream, were you standing next to the victim...

765
01:08:36,680 --> 01:08:38,470
...or looking down at the scene?

766
01:08:38,650 --> 01:08:41,920
Neither. It was like I...

767
01:08:42,180 --> 01:08:44,440
will you please just tell me what's happening?

768
01:08:44,450 --> 01:08:46,940
Everard, Arthur's on guard duty tonight.

769
01:08:46,950 --> 01:08:49,510
Make sure he's found by the right people.

770
01:08:49,520 --> 01:08:51,250
-Sir. -Phineas.

771
01:08:51,260 --> 01:08:53,720
You must go to your portrait at Grimmauld Place.

772
01:08:53,730 --> 01:08:56,520
Tell them that Arthur weasley is gravely injured...

773
01:08:56,530 --> 01:08:58,260
...and his children will be

774
01:08:58,270 --> 01:09:00,710
arriving there soon by Portkey.

775
01:09:00,870 --> 01:09:02,570
They've got him, Albus.

776
01:09:02,580 --> 01:09:04,350
It was close, but they think he'll make it.

777
01:09:04,360 --> 01:09:06,800
What's more, the Dark Lord failed to acquire it.

778
01:09:06,810 --> 01:09:08,870
Oh, thank goodness. Next we need to...

779
01:09:08,880 --> 01:09:10,370
Look at me!

780
01:09:16,580 --> 01:09:19,110
What's happening to me?

781
01:09:26,690 --> 01:09:28,720
You wished to see me, headmaster?

782
01:09:28,730 --> 01:09:31,880
Oh, Severus. I'm afraid we can't wait.

783
01:09:32,390 --> 01:09:33,930
Not even till the morning.

784
01:09:34,030 --> 01:09:37,240
Otherwise, we'll all be vulnerable.

785
01:09:41,710 --> 01:09:43,470
It appears there's a connection...

786
01:09:43,480 --> 01:09:45,970
...between the Dark Lord's mind and your own.

787
01:09:45,980 --> 01:09:48,960
Whether he is, as yet, aware of this connection is

788
01:09:48,970 --> 01:09:50,870
for the moment, unclear.

789
01:09:50,880 --> 01:09:53,710
Pray he remains ignorant.

790
01:09:53,720 --> 01:09:57,290
You mean, if he knows about it, then...

791
01:09:57,460 --> 01:10:02,020
-...he'll be able to read my mind? -Read it, control it...

792
01:10:02,030 --> 01:10:04,050
...unhinge it.

793
01:10:04,060 --> 01:10:07,590
In the past, it was often the Dark Lord's pleasure...

794
01:10:07,600 --> 01:10:09,990
...to invade the minds of his victims...

795
01:10:10,000 --> 01:10:13,900
...creating visions designed to torture them into madness.

796
01:10:14,740 --> 01:10:19,700
Only after extracting the last exquisite ounce of agony...

797
01:10:19,710 --> 01:10:22,640
...only when he had them literally begging for death,

798
01:10:22,650 --> 01:10:24,600
would he finally...

799
01:10:24,740 --> 01:10:25,990
...kill them.

800
01:10:26,350 --> 01:10:28,950
Used properly, the power of occlumency...

801
01:10:28,960 --> 01:10:32,620
...will help shield you from access or influence.

802
01:10:32,630 --> 01:10:37,690
In these lessons, I will attempt to penetrate your mind.

803
01:10:37,970 --> 01:10:41,330
You will attempt to resist.

804
01:10:41,340 --> 01:10:43,100
Prepare yourself.

805
01:10:45,540 --> 01:10:47,070
Legilimens.

806
01:10:54,880 --> 01:10:58,780
Concentrate, Potter. Focus.

807
01:11:24,380 --> 01:11:26,710
Ho, ho, ho. Merry Christmas.

808
01:11:27,210 --> 01:11:30,040
Here we go.

809
01:11:30,050 --> 01:11:32,510
Daddy's back.

810
01:11:35,390 --> 01:11:39,180
Sit down, everybody, sit down. That's it. Now, presents.

811
01:11:39,190 --> 01:11:43,860
And a nice big box for Ron. Big box for you. And...

812
01:11:46,370 --> 01:11:48,730
Fred and George. Come on, open up.

813
01:11:48,740 --> 01:11:51,200
-I want to see your faces. -Yes.

814
01:11:51,210 --> 01:11:53,760
-Try it on. -Thanks, Mum. It's perfect.

815
01:11:53,770 --> 01:11:58,240
-Just what he wanted, actually. -Yeah. Right. Thanks, Mum.

816
01:11:58,250 --> 01:12:01,270
Come on, then, everybody. Let's clear this away.

817
01:12:01,280 --> 01:12:03,470
Oh, Harry, Harry.

818
01:12:03,480 --> 01:12:05,680
There you are.

819
01:12:06,390 --> 01:12:08,520
-Happy christmas. -Thank you.

820
01:12:08,790 --> 01:12:10,810
-Lovely to have you with us. -Thank you.

821
01:12:10,820 --> 01:12:12,950
Now, Daddy. Pass that to Daddy.

822
01:12:12,960 --> 01:12:14,850
-Thank you. -Has everybody got?

823
01:12:14,860 --> 01:12:16,390
Fred? George?

824
01:12:16,400 --> 01:12:19,090
-Hermione. -A christmas toast.

825
01:12:19,100 --> 01:12:21,260
To Mr. Harry Potter...

826
01:12:22,000 --> 01:12:25,140
...without whom I would not be here.

827
01:12:28,410 --> 01:12:30,900
-Harry. -Harry.

828
01:12:30,910 --> 01:12:32,440
Harry.

829
01:12:33,150 --> 01:12:35,910
That is delicious. I shall be needing some more of that.

830
01:12:35,920 --> 01:12:38,580
Daddy, don't forget last christmas.

831
01:12:39,220 --> 01:12:42,250
I can't understand why you don't want to wear it, Ronald.

832
01:12:43,420 --> 01:12:45,420
I look like a bloody idiot, that's why.

833
01:12:45,430 --> 01:12:47,450
No more than usual, Ron.

834
01:12:47,460 --> 01:12:49,590
I don't know why...

835
01:12:55,300 --> 01:13:00,060
Nasty brat, standing there as bold as brass.

836
01:13:00,070 --> 01:13:04,970
Harry Potter, the boy who stopped the Dark Lord.

837
01:13:04,980 --> 01:13:08,270
Friend of Mudbloods and blood-traitors alike.

838
01:13:08,420 --> 01:13:11,170
-If my poor mistress only knew... -Kreacher!

839
01:13:11,180 --> 01:13:14,180
That's enough of your bile. Away with you!

840
01:13:14,190 --> 01:13:16,350
Of course, master.

841
01:13:16,360 --> 01:13:18,380
Kreacher lives to

842
01:13:18,390 --> 01:13:20,830
serve the noble house of Black.

843
01:13:23,360 --> 01:13:25,560
Sorry about that.

844
01:13:25,830 --> 01:13:29,800
He never was very pleasant, even when I was a boy.

845
01:13:29,840 --> 01:13:32,230
Not to me, anyway.

846
01:13:32,770 --> 01:13:34,870
What, you grew up here?

847
01:13:34,880 --> 01:13:37,440
This is my parents' house.

848
01:13:37,480 --> 01:13:41,610
I offered it to Dumbledore as headquarters for the order.

849
01:13:42,450 --> 01:13:46,010
About the only useful thing I've been able to do.

850
01:13:47,120 --> 01:13:49,790
This is the Black family tree.

851
01:13:50,390 --> 01:13:52,680
My deranged cousin.

852
01:13:52,690 --> 01:13:55,590
I hated the lot of them.

853
01:13:55,600 --> 01:14:00,590
My parents with their pure-blood mania.

854
01:14:03,500 --> 01:14:07,600
My mother did that after I ran away.

855
01:14:09,640 --> 01:14:11,810
Charming woman.

856
01:14:12,780 --> 01:14:14,710
I was 16.

857
01:14:15,250 --> 01:14:16,980
Where did you go?

858
01:14:18,750 --> 01:14:20,310
Round your dad's.

859
01:14:21,520 --> 01:14:24,350
I was always welcome at the Potters'.

860
01:14:24,960 --> 01:14:27,990
I see him so much in you, Harry.

861
01:14:28,330 --> 01:14:30,820
You are so very much alike.

862
01:14:31,470 --> 01:14:33,730
I'm not so sure.

863
01:14:34,500 --> 01:14:36,230
Sirius, when I was...

864
01:14:38,770 --> 01:14:41,230
when I saw Mr. Weasley attacked

865
01:14:41,240 --> 01:14:43,220
I wasn't just watching.

866
01:14:44,440 --> 01:14:46,270
I was the snake.

867
01:14:46,810 --> 01:14:49,910
And afterwards, in Dumbledore's office...

868
01:14:49,920 --> 01:14:54,410
...there was a moment when I wanted to...

869
01:14:59,260 --> 01:15:02,790
This connection between me and Voldemort.

870
01:15:02,800 --> 01:15:07,690
What if the reason for it is that I am becoming more like him?

871
01:15:07,730 --> 01:15:12,800
I just feel so angry all the time.

872
01:15:12,810 --> 01:15:17,530
And what if, after everything that I've been through...

873
01:15:17,540 --> 01:15:22,010
...something's gone wrong inside me? What if I'm becoming bad?

874
01:15:23,750 --> 01:15:27,280
I want you to listen to me very carefully, Harry.

875
01:15:28,190 --> 01:15:31,460
You're not a bad person.

876
01:15:31,990 --> 01:15:33,610
You're a very good person

877
01:15:33,610 --> 01:15:36,660
who bad things have happened to.

878
01:15:36,960 --> 01:15:38,390
You understand?

879
01:15:40,200 --> 01:15:43,780
Besides, the world isn't split into

880
01:15:44,390 --> 01:15:45,400
good people and Death Eaters.

881
01:15:45,410 --> 01:15:50,170
We've all got both light and dark inside of us.

882
01:15:50,610 --> 01:15:54,180
What matters is the part we choose to act on.

883
01:15:55,820 --> 01:15:58,410
That's who we really are.

884
01:16:01,860 --> 01:16:03,920
Harry, time to go.

885
01:16:05,390 --> 01:16:09,820
When all this is over, we'll be a proper family.

886
01:16:09,830 --> 01:16:11,720
You'll see.

887
01:16:12,570 --> 01:16:14,230
Come on.

888
01:16:51,370 --> 01:16:52,700
Really?

889
01:16:52,710 --> 01:16:55,500
Harry. Harry.

890
01:16:55,510 --> 01:16:57,740
Hagrid's back.

891
01:17:00,380 --> 01:17:02,510
I'm sorry.

892
01:17:16,430 --> 01:17:19,890
I will say this one last time.

893
01:17:19,900 --> 01:17:22,430
I'm ordering you to tell me where you've been.

894
01:17:22,440 --> 01:17:25,760
I told you. I've been away for me health.

895
01:17:25,810 --> 01:17:27,500
Your health?

896
01:17:27,620 --> 01:17:30,130
Yeah. Bit of fresh air, you know.

897
01:17:30,140 --> 01:17:33,020
Oh, yes. As gamekeeper

898
01:17:33,030 --> 01:17:35,630
fresh air must be difficult to come by.

899
01:17:37,020 --> 01:17:39,680
If I were you, I shouldn't get too used to being back.

900
01:17:39,690 --> 01:17:43,250
In fact, I mightn't bother unpacking at all.

901
01:18:01,910 --> 01:18:05,300
This is top-secret, right?

902
01:18:05,910 --> 01:18:08,440
Dumbledore sent me to parley with the giants.

903
01:18:08,450 --> 01:18:10,240
Giants?

904
01:18:11,180 --> 01:18:12,340
You found them?

905
01:18:12,350 --> 01:18:15,240
Well, they're not that hard to find, to be perfectly honest.

906
01:18:15,250 --> 01:18:17,110
They're so big, see?

907
01:18:17,120 --> 01:18:20,320
I tried to convince them to join the cause.

908
01:18:20,330 --> 01:18:23,620
But I wasn't the only one that was trying to win them over.

909
01:18:23,730 --> 01:18:25,930
-Death Eaters? -Yes.

910
01:18:26,100 --> 01:18:29,730
Trying to persuade them to join You-Know-who.

911
01:18:29,940 --> 01:18:32,460
-Did they? -I gave them Dumbledore's message.

912
01:18:32,470 --> 01:18:34,910
Suppose some of them remember he was friendly to them.

913
01:18:34,920 --> 01:18:36,660
I suppose.

914
01:18:40,180 --> 01:18:41,780
And they did this to you?

915
01:18:42,180 --> 01:18:44,250
Not exactly, no.

916
01:18:44,450 --> 01:18:48,650
Oh, go on, you have it, then, you dozy dog.

917
01:19:02,340 --> 01:19:04,760
It's changing out there.

918
01:19:04,900 --> 01:19:06,760
Just like last time.

919
01:19:07,940 --> 01:19:10,060
There's a storm coming, Harry.

920
01:19:10,310 --> 01:19:13,670
We'd all best be ready when she does.

921
01:19:50,380 --> 01:19:53,580
We have confirmed that 10 high-security prisoners...

922
01:19:53,590 --> 01:19:56,580
...in the early hours of yesterday evening did escape.

923
01:19:56,590 --> 01:20:00,420
And of course, the Muggle prime minister has been alerted to the danger.

924
01:20:00,430 --> 01:20:02,820
We strongly suspect...

925
01:20:03,360 --> 01:20:05,520
...that the breakout was engineered...

926
01:20:05,530 --> 01:20:09,890
...by a man with personal experience in escaping from Azkaban...

927
01:20:09,900 --> 01:20:14,440
...notorious mass murderer Sirius Black...

928
01:20:15,580 --> 01:20:20,240
...cousin of escapee Bellatrix Lestrange.

929
01:20:30,260 --> 01:20:32,720
Dumbledore warned Fudge this could happen.

930
01:20:32,730 --> 01:20:36,050
He's gonna get us all killed just because he can't face the truth.

931
01:20:36,060 --> 01:20:37,490
Harry.

932
01:20:40,900 --> 01:20:43,190
I wanted to apologize.

933
01:20:43,500 --> 01:20:44,860
Now even me

934
01:20:44,870 --> 01:20:47,610
mum says the Prophet's version of things don't add up.

935
01:20:47,840 --> 01:20:54,050
So, what I'm really trying to say is that I believe you.

936
01:21:00,690 --> 01:21:02,580
Neville?

937
01:21:14,870 --> 01:21:17,160
Fourteen years ago...

938
01:21:17,170 --> 01:21:21,600
...a Death Eater named Bellatrix Lestrange...

939
01:21:21,610 --> 01:21:25,110
...used a cruciatus curse on my parents.

940
01:21:25,380 --> 01:21:29,510
She tortured them for information...

941
01:21:29,520 --> 01:21:31,980
...but they never gave in.

942
01:21:33,350 --> 01:21:36,140
I'm quite proud to be their son.

943
01:21:36,820 --> 01:21:38,960
But I'm not sure I'm ready for

944
01:21:38,970 --> 01:21:40,650
everyone to know just yet.

945
01:21:46,630 --> 01:21:49,000
We're gonna make them proud, Neville.

946
01:21:49,400 --> 01:21:50,890
That's a promise.

947
01:21:55,010 --> 01:21:58,870
Make it a powerful memory, the happiest you can remember.

948
01:21:58,880 --> 01:22:02,470
Allow it to fill you up. Keep trying, Seamus.

949
01:22:02,480 --> 01:22:04,880
George, your turn now.

950
01:22:05,250 --> 01:22:07,850
Expecto Patronum.

951
01:22:08,490 --> 01:22:12,080
A full-bodied Patronus is the most difficult to produce...

952
01:22:12,090 --> 01:22:16,090
...but shield forms can also be equally useful against a variety of opponents.

953
01:22:16,100 --> 01:22:17,620
Wow, that was really good.

954
01:22:18,030 --> 01:22:19,760
Fantastic, Ginny.

955
01:22:19,770 --> 01:22:21,190
Just remember

956
01:22:21,200 --> 01:22:24,390
your Patronus can only protect you for as long as you stay focused.

957
01:22:24,400 --> 01:22:26,570
So focus, Luna.

958
01:22:29,980 --> 01:22:31,840
Think of the happiest thing you can.

959
01:22:31,850 --> 01:22:33,970
Expecto Patronum.

960
01:22:33,980 --> 01:22:37,010
-I'm trying. -I know. It's good.

961
01:22:37,020 --> 01:22:39,400
This is really advanced stuff, guys.

962
01:22:39,410 --> 01:22:41,210
You're doing so well.

963
01:22:42,020 --> 01:22:44,720
Expecto Patronum.

964
01:23:26,270 --> 01:23:29,090
I'll make short work of this.

965
01:23:30,140 --> 01:23:32,430
Bombarda Maxima.

966
01:23:50,420 --> 01:23:52,090
Get them.

967
01:23:52,230 --> 01:23:53,850
Been watching them for weeks.

968
01:23:53,860 --> 01:23:56,220
And see, "Dumbledore's Army"...

969
01:23:56,230 --> 01:24:00,230
...proof of what I've been telling you right from the beginning, cornelius.

970
01:24:01,300 --> 01:24:03,530
All your fear-mongering about You-Know-who...

971
01:24:03,540 --> 01:24:05,230
...never fooled us for a minute.

972
01:24:05,240 --> 01:24:07,460
We saw your lies for what they were:

973
01:24:07,470 --> 01:24:11,470
A smokescreen for your bid to seize control of the Ministry.

974
01:24:11,480 --> 01:24:12,640
Naturally.

975
01:24:12,650 --> 01:24:15,340
No, professor. He had nothing to do with it. It was me.

976
01:24:15,350 --> 01:24:19,180
Most noble of you, Harry, to shield me, but as has been pointed out...

977
01:24:19,190 --> 01:24:21,320
...the parchment clearly says

978
01:24:21,330 --> 01:24:24,250
"Dumbledore's Army," not "Potter's."

979
01:24:24,260 --> 01:24:26,980
I instructed Harry to form this organization.

980
01:24:26,990 --> 01:24:31,020
And I, and I alone, am responsible for its activities.

981
01:24:31,030 --> 01:24:32,620
Dispatch an owl to the Daily Prophet.

982
01:24:32,630 --> 01:24:35,330
If we hurry, we should still make the morning edition.

983
01:24:35,340 --> 01:24:40,300
Dawlish, Shacklebolt, you will escort Dumbledore...

984
01:24:40,310 --> 01:24:42,040
...to Azkaban...

985
01:24:42,980 --> 01:24:48,300
...to await trial for conspiracy and sedition.

986
01:24:48,310 --> 01:24:51,550
I thought we might hit this little snag.

987
01:24:52,420 --> 01:24:56,150
You seem to be laboring under the delusion that I'm going to...

988
01:24:56,420 --> 01:24:58,010
what was the phrase?

989
01:24:58,020 --> 01:24:59,780
Come quietly.

990
01:24:59,790 --> 01:25:01,790
Well, I can tell you this:

991
01:25:01,930 --> 01:25:04,390
I have no intention of going to Azkaban.

992
01:25:04,400 --> 01:25:05,960
Enough of this.

993
01:25:06,170 --> 01:25:07,560
Take him.

994
01:25:20,110 --> 01:25:24,640
Well, you may not like him, minister...

995
01:25:24,650 --> 01:25:27,080
...but you can't deny...

996
01:25:27,320 --> 01:25:30,350
...Dumbledore has got style.

997
01:25:54,150 --> 01:25:58,940
Boys and girls are not permitted to be within eight inches of each other.

998
01:25:58,950 --> 01:26:02,550
Those wishing to join the Inquisitorial Squad for extra credit...

999
01:26:02,560 --> 01:26:07,750
Students will be submitted to questioning about suspected illicit activities.

1000
01:26:07,760 --> 01:26:12,360
Any student in noncompliance will be expelled.

1001
01:27:23,270 --> 01:27:25,160
Harry.

1002
01:27:31,810 --> 01:27:35,370
You did everything you could. No one could win against that old hag.

1003
01:27:35,380 --> 01:27:38,050
Even Dumbledore didn't see this coming.

1004
01:27:38,650 --> 01:27:40,980
Harry, if it's anyone's fault, it's ours.

1005
01:27:40,990 --> 01:27:43,250
Yeah, we talked you into it.

1006
01:27:43,260 --> 01:27:45,520
Yeah, but I agreed.

1007
01:27:45,790 --> 01:27:50,220
I tried so hard to help, and all it's done is make things worse.

1008
01:27:51,960 --> 01:27:54,700
Anyway, that doesn't matter anymore.

1009
01:27:55,470 --> 01:27:59,830
Because I don't want to play anymore. All it does is make you care too much.

1010
01:27:59,840 --> 01:28:02,670
And the more you care, the more you have to lose.

1011
01:28:02,680 --> 01:28:06,140
-So maybe it's just better to... -To what?

1012
01:28:08,080 --> 01:28:10,310
To go it alone.

1013
01:28:16,360 --> 01:28:18,320
Hagrid.

1014
01:28:21,760 --> 01:28:24,350
Any idea where he's taking us?

1015
01:28:24,360 --> 01:28:27,720
Hagrid, why can't you just tell us?

1016
01:28:35,740 --> 01:28:38,570
I've never seen the centaurs so riled.

1017
01:28:38,580 --> 01:28:41,440
And they're dangerous at the best of times.

1018
01:28:42,080 --> 01:28:44,570
The Ministry restricts their territory much more...

1019
01:28:44,580 --> 01:28:46,940
...they'll have a full uprising on their hands.

1020
01:28:46,950 --> 01:28:48,780
Hagrid, what's going on?

1021
01:28:48,790 --> 01:28:51,980
I'm sorry to be so mysterious, you three.

1022
01:28:51,990 --> 01:28:56,450
I wouldn't be bothering you at all with it, but with Dumbledore gone...

1023
01:28:56,800 --> 01:29:00,120
...l'll likely be getting the sack any day now.

1024
01:29:00,130 --> 01:29:03,920
And I just couldn't leave without telling someone about him.

1025
01:29:07,840 --> 01:29:09,770
Grawpy.

1026
01:29:11,880 --> 01:29:14,270
Down here, you great buffoon.

1027
01:29:20,320 --> 01:29:22,310
Grawpy.

1028
01:29:22,790 --> 01:29:24,780
Brought you some company.

1029
01:29:36,840 --> 01:29:39,260
I couldn't just leave him, because...

1030
01:29:39,270 --> 01:29:41,160
Because he's my brother.

1031
01:29:41,170 --> 01:29:42,470
Blimey.

1032
01:29:42,480 --> 01:29:44,670
Well, half brother, really.

1033
01:29:44,680 --> 01:29:47,630
He's completely harmless, just like I said.

1034
01:29:47,930 --> 01:29:50,270
Little high-spirited, is all.

1035
01:29:52,080 --> 01:29:54,580
-Grawpy, that is not polite. -Hagrid, do something.

1036
01:29:54,590 --> 01:29:55,660
We talked about this.

1037
01:29:55,670 --> 01:29:57,250
You do not grab, do you?

1038
01:29:57,260 --> 01:29:59,580
That's your new friend, Hermione.

1039
01:29:59,590 --> 01:30:01,190
Grawpy.

1040
01:30:05,200 --> 01:30:06,690
Grawp.

1041
01:30:08,430 --> 01:30:11,790
Put me down.

1042
01:30:15,170 --> 01:30:17,030
Now.

1043
01:30:28,890 --> 01:30:30,280
You all right?

1044
01:30:31,290 --> 01:30:33,250
Fine.

1045
01:30:33,360 --> 01:30:35,820
Just needs a firm hand, is all.

1046
01:30:35,830 --> 01:30:38,530
I think you've got an admirer.

1047
01:30:40,730 --> 01:30:43,190
You just stay away from her, all right?

1048
01:31:13,030 --> 01:31:16,060
He gets his own food and all.

1049
01:31:17,040 --> 01:31:20,400
It's company he'll be needing when I'm gone.

1050
01:31:21,440 --> 01:31:23,970
You will look after him, won't you?

1051
01:31:24,180 --> 01:31:27,170
I'm the only family he's got.

1052
01:31:40,460 --> 01:31:42,820
Feeling sentimental?

1053
01:31:45,600 --> 01:31:49,730
-That's private. -Not to me.

1054
01:31:49,740 --> 01:31:53,530
And not to the Dark Lord, if you don't improve.

1055
01:31:55,670 --> 01:31:57,930
Every memory he has access to

1056
01:31:57,940 --> 01:31:59,100
is a weapon he can use against you.

1057
01:31:59,110 --> 01:32:03,440
You won't last two seconds if he invades your mind.

1058
01:32:04,320 --> 01:32:06,740
You're just like your father.

1059
01:32:06,750 --> 01:32:08,710
Lazy, arrogant.

1060
01:32:08,720 --> 01:32:11,110
-Don't say a word against my father. -Weak.

1061
01:32:11,120 --> 01:32:13,920
-I'm not weak. -Then prove it.

1062
01:32:13,930 --> 01:32:16,020
Control your emotions.

1063
01:32:16,030 --> 01:32:19,260
Discipline your mind.

1064
01:32:21,800 --> 01:32:23,300
Legilimens.

1065
01:32:30,210 --> 01:32:31,470
Harry.

1066
01:32:31,480 --> 01:32:33,510
Sirius.

1067
01:32:33,880 --> 01:32:35,510
I may vomit.

1068
01:32:35,510 --> 01:32:36,840
Stop it.

1069
01:32:37,680 --> 01:32:40,280
Is this what you call control?

1070
01:32:40,490 --> 01:32:41,760
We've been at it for hours.

1071
01:32:41,770 --> 01:32:43,550
If I could just rest.

1072
01:32:43,720 --> 01:32:47,420
The Dark Lord isn't resting.

1073
01:32:48,760 --> 01:32:50,820
You and Black, you're two of a kind.

1074
01:32:50,830 --> 01:32:53,260
Sentimental children forever whining about

1075
01:32:53,270 --> 01:32:54,960
how bitterly unfair your lives have been.

1076
01:32:54,970 --> 01:32:57,060
Well, it may have escaped your notice

1077
01:32:57,070 --> 01:32:58,760
but life isn't fair.

1078
01:32:58,770 --> 01:33:00,750
Your blessed father knew that.

1079
01:33:00,760 --> 01:33:02,630
In fact, he frequently saw to it.

1080
01:33:02,640 --> 01:33:06,170
-My father was a great man. -Your father was a swine.

1081
01:33:06,710 --> 01:33:08,500
-Legilimens. -Protego.

1082
01:33:13,790 --> 01:33:15,480
Come on, Moony, Padfoot.

1083
01:33:15,490 --> 01:33:17,710
Snape. Expelliarmus.

1084
01:33:17,720 --> 01:33:19,850
Nice one, James.

1085
01:33:19,930 --> 01:33:22,380
-Dad. -Impedimenta.

1086
01:33:22,390 --> 01:33:24,550
Snivellus Greasy. Snivellus Greasy.

1087
01:33:24,560 --> 01:33:27,390
Right. Who wants to see me take off Snivelly's trousers?

1088
01:33:27,400 --> 01:33:29,830
Snivellus Greasy. Snivellus Greasy.

1089
01:33:29,840 --> 01:33:31,330
Enough.

1090
01:33:33,010 --> 01:33:34,900
Enough.

1091
01:33:43,120 --> 01:33:45,880
Your lessons are at an end.

1092
01:33:45,890 --> 01:33:47,180
L...

1093
01:33:47,190 --> 01:33:50,750
Get out.

1094
01:34:07,670 --> 01:34:10,000
-What's your name? -Michael.

1095
01:34:10,010 --> 01:34:12,070
Your hand's gonna be fine, Michael.

1096
01:34:12,080 --> 01:34:15,270
Yeah. It's not as bad as it seems. See?

1097
01:34:15,280 --> 01:34:17,470
It's fading already.

1098
01:34:17,480 --> 01:34:22,520
You can hardly see ours anymore, and the pain stops after a while.

1099
01:34:29,600 --> 01:34:32,490
As I told you once before, Mr. Potter...

1100
01:34:32,500 --> 01:34:36,560
...naughty children deserve to be punished.

1101
01:34:39,340 --> 01:34:40,830
You know, George...

1102
01:34:40,840 --> 01:34:44,670
...l've always felt our futures lay outside the world of academic achievement.

1103
01:34:44,680 --> 01:34:48,540
Fred, I've been thinking exactly the same thing.

1104
01:36:01,190 --> 01:36:03,150
All right, professor!

1105
01:36:11,630 --> 01:36:13,690
Here you go.

1106
01:36:38,360 --> 01:36:40,490
Ready when you are.

1107
01:38:05,940 --> 01:38:09,370
I need that prophecy.

1108
01:38:09,380 --> 01:38:11,480
You'll have to kill me.

1109
01:38:12,050 --> 01:38:16,780
Oh, I will. But first, you will fetch it for me.

1110
01:38:16,790 --> 01:38:18,780
Crucio.

1111
01:38:21,030 --> 01:38:23,090
Crucio.

1112
01:38:34,170 --> 01:38:35,800
Sirius.

1113
01:38:35,810 --> 01:38:36,970
Harry, are you sure?

1114
01:38:36,980 --> 01:38:39,940
I saw it. It's just like with Mr. Weasley.

1115
01:38:39,950 --> 01:38:41,640
It's the door I've been dreaming about.

1116
01:38:41,650 --> 01:38:43,870
I couldn't remember where I'd seen it before.

1117
01:38:43,880 --> 01:38:45,970
Sirius said Voldemort was after something.

1118
01:38:45,980 --> 01:38:49,450
Something he didn't have the last time, in the Department of Mysteries.

1119
01:38:49,460 --> 01:38:51,690
Harry, please, just listen.

1120
01:38:52,890 --> 01:38:55,180
What if Voldemort meant for you to see this?

1121
01:38:56,200 --> 01:38:59,490
What if he's only hurting Sirius because he's trying to get to you?

1122
01:38:59,500 --> 01:39:03,160
What if he is? I'm supposed to just let him die?

1123
01:39:03,170 --> 01:39:06,960
Hermione, he's the only family I've got left.

1124
01:39:09,270 --> 01:39:10,760
What do we do?

1125
01:39:11,680 --> 01:39:13,470
We'll have to use the Floo Network.

1126
01:39:13,480 --> 01:39:15,700
Umbridge has the chimneys under surveillance.

1127
01:39:15,710 --> 01:39:17,570
Not all of them.

1128
01:39:20,090 --> 01:39:21,720
Alohomora.

1129
01:39:32,660 --> 01:39:34,520
Alert the order if you can.

1130
01:39:34,530 --> 01:39:38,260
-Are you mental? We're going with you. -It's too dangerous.

1131
01:39:38,270 --> 01:39:42,360
When are you going to get it into your head? We're in this together.

1132
01:39:42,370 --> 01:39:45,470
That you are.

1133
01:39:45,480 --> 01:39:48,640
Caught this one trying to help the weasley girl.

1134
01:39:53,350 --> 01:39:55,610
You were going to Dumbledore, weren't you?

1135
01:39:55,620 --> 01:39:57,810
-No. -Liar.

1136
01:39:57,820 --> 01:40:00,820
-You sent for me, headmistress? -Snape, yes.

1137
01:40:00,830 --> 01:40:03,070
The time has come for answers

1138
01:40:03,080 --> 01:40:04,990
whether he wants to give them to me or not.

1139
01:40:05,030 --> 01:40:06,620
Have you brought the Veritaserum?

1140
01:40:06,630 --> 01:40:09,490
I'm afraid you've used up all my stores interrogating students.

1141
01:40:09,500 --> 01:40:12,930
The last of it on Miss Chang.

1142
01:40:16,710 --> 01:40:18,330
Unless you wish to poison him...

1143
01:40:18,340 --> 01:40:19,330
And I assure you

1144
01:40:19,340 --> 01:40:22,600
I would have the greatest sympathy if you did.

1145
01:40:23,380 --> 01:40:25,620
I cannot help you.

1146
01:40:27,750 --> 01:40:29,750
He's got Padfoot.

1147
01:40:30,490 --> 01:40:34,280
He's got Padfoot at the place where it's hidden.

1148
01:40:34,460 --> 01:40:36,750
Padfoot? What is Padfoot? Where what is hidden?

1149
01:40:36,760 --> 01:40:38,590
What is he talking about, Snape?

1150
01:40:44,970 --> 01:40:47,260
No idea.

1151
01:40:51,480 --> 01:40:53,330
Very well.

1152
01:40:54,050 --> 01:40:56,680
You give me no choice, Potter.

1153
01:40:56,750 --> 01:40:59,880
As this is an issue of Ministry security...

1154
01:40:59,890 --> 01:41:02,240
...you leave me with...

1155
01:41:02,690 --> 01:41:04,960
...no alternative.

1156
01:41:05,460 --> 01:41:07,820
The cruciatus curse ought to loosen your tongue.

1157
01:41:07,830 --> 01:41:08,980
That's illegal.

1158
01:41:08,990 --> 01:41:13,060
What cornelius doesn't know won't hurt him.

1159
01:41:19,870 --> 01:41:21,700
Tell her, Harry!

1160
01:41:22,910 --> 01:41:24,640
Tell me what?

1161
01:41:25,540 --> 01:41:27,840
Well, if you won't tell her where it is...

1162
01:41:28,210 --> 01:41:30,280
...I will.

1163
01:41:31,620 --> 01:41:33,710
Where what is?

1164
01:41:34,620 --> 01:41:37,220
Dumbledore's secret weapon.

1165
01:41:41,930 --> 01:41:43,620
How much further?

1166
01:41:43,630 --> 01:41:45,590
Not far.

1167
01:41:47,300 --> 01:41:51,300
It had to be somewhere students wouldn't find it accidentally.

1168
01:41:55,340 --> 01:41:56,970
What are you doing?

1169
01:41:56,980 --> 01:41:59,070
Lmprovising.

1170
01:42:07,290 --> 01:42:09,180
Well?

1171
01:42:10,190 --> 01:42:12,620
Where is this weapon?

1172
01:42:17,230 --> 01:42:19,790
There isn't one, is there?

1173
01:42:22,270 --> 01:42:24,730
You were trying to trick me.

1174
01:42:28,640 --> 01:42:30,500
You know...

1175
01:42:31,610 --> 01:42:33,940
...I really hate children.

1176
01:42:49,230 --> 01:42:53,960
You have no business here, centaur. This is a Ministry matter.

1177
01:42:56,330 --> 01:42:58,160
Lower your weapons.

1178
01:42:58,170 --> 01:43:01,160
I warn you, under the law

1179
01:43:01,170 --> 01:43:04,380
as creatures of near-human intelligence...

1180
01:43:04,560 --> 01:43:05,370
Protego.

1181
01:43:05,380 --> 01:43:07,000
How dare you?

1182
01:43:07,150 --> 01:43:09,270
Filthy half-breed.

1183
01:43:09,450 --> 01:43:11,040
Incarcerous.

1184
01:43:23,660 --> 01:43:26,420
Please. Please stop it. Please.

1185
01:43:26,430 --> 01:43:31,400
Now, enough. I will have order.

1186
01:43:39,950 --> 01:43:42,670
You filthy animal.

1187
01:43:42,680 --> 01:43:45,810
Do you know who I am?

1188
01:43:45,820 --> 01:43:48,810
Leave him alone. It's not his fault.

1189
01:43:48,820 --> 01:43:50,990
No, he doesn't understand.

1190
01:43:58,360 --> 01:44:01,990
Potter, do something. Tell them I mean no harm.

1191
01:44:02,000 --> 01:44:04,090
I'm sorry, professor.

1192
01:44:04,100 --> 01:44:06,060
But I must not tell lies.

1193
01:44:06,070 --> 01:44:07,230
What are you doing?

1194
01:44:07,240 --> 01:44:11,530
I am Senior Undersecretary Dolores Jane Umbridge.

1195
01:44:11,540 --> 01:44:14,040
Let me go!

1196
01:44:16,410 --> 01:44:18,370
Thank you, Grawp.

1197
01:44:18,380 --> 01:44:22,180
Hermione. Hermione, Sirius.

1198
01:44:30,160 --> 01:44:31,420
How'd you get away?

1199
01:44:31,430 --> 01:44:33,890
Puking Pastilles. It wasn't pretty.

1200
01:44:33,900 --> 01:44:36,190
Told them I was hungry, wanted some sweets.

1201
01:44:36,200 --> 01:44:39,060
They told me to bugger off and ate the lot themselves.

1202
01:44:39,600 --> 01:44:41,390
That was clever, Ron.

1203
01:44:41,940 --> 01:44:44,600
-Has been known to happen. -It was brilliant.

1204
01:44:44,610 --> 01:44:46,700
So how are we getting to London?

1205
01:44:47,780 --> 01:44:51,600
Look, it's not that I don't appreciate everything you've done, all of you...

1206
01:44:51,750 --> 01:44:55,010
...but I've got you into enough trouble as it is.

1207
01:44:55,020 --> 01:44:58,290
Dumbledore's Army's supposed to be about doing something real.

1208
01:44:58,320 --> 01:45:00,750
Or was that all just words to you?

1209
01:45:02,320 --> 01:45:05,820
Maybe you don't have to do this all by yourself, mate.

1210
01:45:10,430 --> 01:45:12,890
So how are we going to get to London?

1211
01:45:14,000 --> 01:45:16,530
We fly, of course.

1212
01:46:07,290 --> 01:46:10,250
Department of Mysteries.

1213
01:46:18,300 --> 01:46:20,300
This is it.

1214
01:47:12,990 --> 01:47:15,620
92 93
Ninety-two. Ninety-three.

1215
01:47:33,240 --> 01:47:36,310
-He should be here. -Harry.

1216
01:47:38,710 --> 01:47:40,310
It's got your name on it.

1217
01:48:05,210 --> 01:48:10,180
The one with the power to vanquish the Dark Lord approaches.

1218
01:48:10,410 --> 01:48:13,010
And the Dark Lord shall mark him as his equal...

1219
01:48:13,020 --> 01:48:16,110
...but he shall have power the Dark Lord knows not.

1220
01:48:21,460 --> 01:48:27,130
For neither can live while the other survives.

1221
01:48:29,330 --> 01:48:30,720
Harry.

1222
01:48:40,910 --> 01:48:42,570
Where's Sirius?

1223
01:48:42,580 --> 01:48:47,980
You know, you really should learn to tell the difference between dreams...

1224
01:48:50,590 --> 01:48:53,050
...and reality.

1225
01:48:54,020 --> 01:48:59,260
You saw only what the Dark Lord wanted you to see.

1226
01:48:59,660 --> 01:49:01,320
Now, hand me the prophecy.

1227
01:49:01,330 --> 01:49:03,720
If you do anything to us, I'll break it.

1228
01:49:06,200 --> 01:49:08,930
He knows how to play.

1229
01:49:08,940 --> 01:49:12,900
Itty, bitty baby.

1230
01:49:12,910 --> 01:49:14,440
Potter.

1231
01:49:14,680 --> 01:49:16,740
Bellatrix Lestrange.

1232
01:49:16,750 --> 01:49:20,040
Neville Longbottom, is it? How's Mum and Dad?

1233
01:49:20,050 --> 01:49:22,210
Better, now they're about to be avenged.

1234
01:49:24,550 --> 01:49:29,920
Now, let's everybody just calm down...

1235
01:49:29,930 --> 01:49:31,480
...shall we?

1236
01:49:31,490 --> 01:49:34,120
All we want is that prophecy.

1237
01:49:34,130 --> 01:49:36,990
Why did Voldemort need me to come and get this?

1238
01:49:37,000 --> 01:49:38,430
You dare speak his name?

1239
01:49:39,670 --> 01:49:41,850
You filthy half-blood!

1240
01:49:41,860 --> 01:49:43,360
It's all right. He's just a curious lad

1241
01:49:43,370 --> 01:49:44,700
aren't you?

1242
01:49:45,970 --> 01:49:51,600
Prophecies can only be retrieved by those about whom they are made.

1243
01:49:51,610 --> 01:49:54,640
Which is lucky for you, really.

1244
01:49:58,120 --> 01:50:00,550
Haven't you always wondered...

1245
01:50:00,560 --> 01:50:06,050
...what was the reason for the connection between you and the Dark Lord?

1246
01:50:06,500 --> 01:50:09,150
Why he was unable to kill you...

1247
01:50:09,160 --> 01:50:11,990
...when you were just an infant?

1248
01:50:13,070 --> 01:50:18,170
Don't you want to know the secret of your scar?

1249
01:50:18,810 --> 01:50:23,510
All the answers are there, Potter, in your hand.

1250
01:50:24,410 --> 01:50:26,700
All you have to do...

1251
01:50:26,980 --> 01:50:29,220
...is give it to me.

1252
01:50:29,220 --> 01:50:32,820
Then I can show you everything.

1253
01:50:41,260 --> 01:50:43,360
I've waited 14 years.

1254
01:50:43,670 --> 01:50:45,260
I know.

1255
01:50:46,270 --> 01:50:48,220
I guess I can wait a little longer.

1256
01:50:48,230 --> 01:50:49,360
Now. Stupefy.

1257
01:50:49,370 --> 01:50:51,100
Stupefy.

1258
01:51:06,960 --> 01:51:08,240
Levicorpus.

1259
01:51:14,500 --> 01:51:16,690
Petrificus Totalus.

1260
01:51:16,700 --> 01:51:18,800
Well done, Neville.

1261
01:51:26,940 --> 01:51:28,800
Stupefy.

1262
01:51:30,250 --> 01:51:31,770
-Stupefy. -Stupefy.

1263
01:51:42,620 --> 01:51:44,820
Stupefy.

1264
01:51:52,070 --> 01:51:54,670
Reducto.

1265
01:52:10,390 --> 01:52:12,780
Get back to the door.

1266
01:52:47,790 --> 01:52:52,580
Department of Mysteries. They got that bit right, didn't they?

1267
01:52:57,500 --> 01:52:59,700
The voices.

1268
01:52:59,970 --> 01:53:02,290
Can you tell what they're saying?

1269
01:53:03,670 --> 01:53:06,130
There aren't any voices, Harry.

1270
01:53:06,580 --> 01:53:08,500
Let's get out of here.

1271
01:53:08,510 --> 01:53:10,400
I hear them too.

1272
01:53:13,220 --> 01:53:16,140
Harry, it's just an empty archway.

1273
01:53:18,620 --> 01:53:20,320
Please, Harry.

1274
01:53:20,790 --> 01:53:22,950
Get behind me.

1275
01:54:09,200 --> 01:54:12,060
Did you actually believe...

1276
01:54:12,070 --> 01:54:16,970
...or were you truly naive enough to think...

1277
01:54:17,280 --> 01:54:22,710
...that children stood a chance against us?

1278
01:54:25,920 --> 01:54:29,950
I'll make this simple for you, Potter.

1279
01:54:33,360 --> 01:54:36,860
Give me the prophecy now...

1280
01:54:36,870 --> 01:54:41,160
...or watch your friends die.

1281
01:54:53,780 --> 01:54:55,480
Don't give it to him, Harry.

1282
01:55:21,480 --> 01:55:24,540
Get away from my godson.

1283
01:55:54,340 --> 01:55:57,470
Now, listen to me. Take the others and get out of here.

1284
01:55:57,480 --> 01:55:59,370
What? No, I'm staying with you.

1285
01:55:59,380 --> 01:56:02,410
You've done beautifully.

1286
01:56:02,750 --> 01:56:04,580
Now, let me take it from here.

1287
01:56:04,590 --> 01:56:05,880
Black.

1288
01:56:32,750 --> 01:56:34,240
Expelliarmus!

1289
01:56:34,250 --> 01:56:35,880
Nice one, James.

1290
01:56:42,820 --> 01:56:44,590
Avada Kedavra.

1291
01:57:04,510 --> 01:57:07,110
No. No.

1292
01:57:30,770 --> 01:57:33,730
I killed Sirius Black.

1293
01:57:34,410 --> 01:57:36,680
-You coming to get me? -Crucio.

1294
01:57:48,720 --> 01:57:52,020
You've got to mean it, Harry.

1295
01:57:52,030 --> 01:57:57,190
She killed him. She deserves it.

1296
01:57:59,630 --> 01:58:03,130
You know the spell, Harry.

1297
01:58:14,380 --> 01:58:16,310
Do it.

1298
01:58:23,690 --> 01:58:26,960
So weak.

1299
01:58:33,440 --> 01:58:36,800
It was foolish of you to come here tonight, Tom.

1300
01:58:36,810 --> 01:58:39,000
The Aurors are on their way.

1301
01:58:39,010 --> 01:58:43,200
By which time I shall be gone, and you...

1302
01:58:44,450 --> 01:58:46,840
...shall be dead.

1303
02:01:00,850 --> 02:01:03,050
You've lost, old man.

1304
02:01:22,900 --> 02:01:24,190
Harry.

1305
02:01:28,040 --> 02:01:29,830
So weak.

1306
02:01:30,040 --> 02:01:32,570
So vulnerable.

1307
02:01:36,580 --> 02:01:37,870
Look at me.

1308
02:01:40,120 --> 02:01:44,520
Harry, it isn't how you are alike.

1309
02:01:44,530 --> 02:01:47,320
It's how you are not.

1310
02:01:51,970 --> 02:01:53,760
Harry?

1311
02:02:25,870 --> 02:02:28,030
You're the weak one...

1312
02:02:28,040 --> 02:02:32,370
...and you'll never know love or friendship.

1313
02:02:35,480 --> 02:02:38,680
And I feel sorry for you.

1314
02:03:01,440 --> 02:03:05,190
You're a fool, Harry Potter.

1315
02:03:05,840 --> 02:03:11,270
And you will lose everything.

1316
02:03:25,930 --> 02:03:27,890
He's back.

1317
02:04:35,330 --> 02:04:37,160
I know how you feel, Harry.

1318
02:04:37,170 --> 02:04:39,060
No, you don't.

1319
02:04:44,410 --> 02:04:45,960
It's my fault.

1320
02:04:45,970 --> 02:04:49,540
No, the fault is mine.

1321
02:04:50,240 --> 02:04:52,370
I knew it was only a matter of time...

1322
02:04:52,380 --> 02:04:55,540
...before Voldemort made the connection between you.

1323
02:04:56,050 --> 02:05:00,480
I thought by distancing myself from you, as I have done all year...

1324
02:05:00,490 --> 02:05:06,020
...he'd be less tempted, and therefore you might be more protected.

1325
02:05:08,530 --> 02:05:12,160
The prophecy said:

1326
02:05:12,470 --> 02:05:16,730
"Neither one can live while the other one survives."

1327
02:05:17,770 --> 02:05:24,140
It means one of us is gonna have to kill the other, in the end.

1328
02:05:25,850 --> 02:05:27,710
Yes.

1329
02:05:27,880 --> 02:05:29,610
Why didn't you tell me?

1330
02:05:29,620 --> 02:05:33,380
For the same reason you tried to save Sirius.

1331
02:05:33,390 --> 02:05:36,120
The same reason your friends saved you.

1332
02:05:36,660 --> 02:05:40,350
After all these years, after all you've suffered...

1333
02:05:40,360 --> 02:05:43,560
...I didn't want to cause you any more pain.

1334
02:05:44,730 --> 02:05:47,160
I cared too much about you.

1335
02:06:11,730 --> 02:06:14,190
How come you're not at the feast?

1336
02:06:14,200 --> 02:06:18,920
Lost all my possessions. Apparently people have been hiding them.

1337
02:06:18,930 --> 02:06:20,090
That's awful.

1338
02:06:20,100 --> 02:06:22,160
Oh, it's all good fun.

1339
02:06:22,170 --> 02:06:25,800
But as it's the last night, I really do need them back.

1340
02:06:25,810 --> 02:06:28,470
Do you want any help finding them?

1341
02:06:31,080 --> 02:06:34,580
I'm sorry about your godfather, Harry.

1342
02:06:41,320 --> 02:06:43,550
Are you sure you don't want any help looking?

1343
02:06:43,560 --> 02:06:45,380
That's all right.

1344
02:06:45,390 --> 02:06:47,950
Anyway, my mum always said...

1345
02:06:47,960 --> 02:06:49,620
...the things we lose have a way

1346
02:06:49,630 --> 02:06:51,520
of coming back to us in the end.

1347
02:06:54,840 --> 02:06:58,400
If not always in the way we expect.

1348
02:06:59,610 --> 02:07:02,600
Think I'll just go have some pudding.

1349
02:07:37,980 --> 02:07:41,040
I've been thinking about something Dumbledore said to me.

1350
02:07:41,050 --> 02:07:43,040
What's that?

1351
02:07:43,350 --> 02:07:46,280
That even though we've got a fight ahead of us...

1352
02:07:46,290 --> 02:07:49,550
...we've got one thing that Voldemort doesn't have.

1353
02:07:49,560 --> 02:07:51,350
Yeah?

1354
02:07:52,960 --> 02:07:55,630
Something worth fighting for.

